By early 2024, Musk had become a vocal and financial supporter of Donald Trump.<ref>{{Cite news |date=July 29, 2024 |title=How Elon Musk came to endorse Donald Trump |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2024/07/29/musk-trump-endorsement-immigration/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240919110730/https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2024/07/29/musk-trump-endorsement-immigration/ |archive-date=September 19, 2024 |access-date=November 9, 2024 |newspaper=The Washington Post}}</ref> In July 2024, minutes after the [[Attempted assassination of Donald Trump in Pennsylvania|attempted assassination of Donald Trump]], Musk [[List of Donald Trump 2024 presidential campaign endorsements|endorsed him for president]] saying; "I fully endorse President Trump and hope for his rapid recovery."<ref>{{Cite news |title=Elon Musk says he 'fully' endorses Donald Trump after shots fired during campaign rally |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-endorses-trump-after-pennsylvania-rally-incident-2024-7 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241112210339/https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-endorses-trump-after-pennsylvania-rally-incident-2024-7 |archive-date=November 12, 2024 |access-date=November 19, 2024 |website=[[Business Insider]]}}</ref><ref name="fucked">{{cite news |last1=Rogers |first1=Alex |last2=Morris |first2=Stephen |last3=Inagaki |first3=Kana |year=2024 |title=Elon Musk's riskiest bet yet: Donald Trump |url=https://on.ft.com/406cj3B |website=[[Financial Times]] |quote="If he loses, I'm fucked"}}</ref> During the [[Donald Trump 2024 presidential campaign|presidential campaign]], Musk joined Trump on stage at a campaign rally,<ref>{{Cite news |last=Kinnard |first=Meg |date=October 5, 2024 |title=Elon Musk makes his first appearance at a Trump rally and casts the election in dire terms |url=https://apnews.com/article/elon-musk-donald-trump-rally-butler-election-f718967ec29431a2b9858b1121e70da1 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241006061925/https://apnews.com/article/elon-musk-donald-trump-rally-butler-election-f718967ec29431a2b9858b1121e70da1 |archive-date=October 6, 2024 |access-date=October 6, 2024 |publisher=Associated Press |language=en}}</ref> and during the campaign promoted conspiracy theories and falsehoods about Democrats, [[Election denial movement in the United States|election fraud]]<ref name="Meyer 11012024">{{Cite news |last=Meyer |first=Josh |date=November 1, 2024 |title=Fake video of Georgia voter fraud is Russian misinformation, US officials say |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/11/01/georgia-voter-fraud-video-fake-russia/75993122007/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241107014209/https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/11/01/georgia-voter-fraud-video-fake-russia/75993122007/ |archive-date=November 7, 2024 |access-date=November 3, 2024 |work=USA Today}}</ref> and immigration, in support of Trump.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Tenbarge |first1=Kat |last2=Goggin |first2=Ben |last3=Barnett |first3=Emma |date=October 17, 2024 |title=Musk pushes debunked Dominion voting conspiracy theory at first Pennsylvania appearance |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/musk-pushes-debunked-dominion-voting-conspiracy-theory-campaign-appear-rcna175985 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241116230513/https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/musk-pushes-debunked-dominion-voting-conspiracy-theory-campaign-appear-rcna175985 |archive-date=November 16, 2024 |access-date=November 19, 2024 |publisher=NBC News}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Ingram |first1=Julia |last2=May |first2=Madeleine |date=October 21, 2024 |title=The X factor: How Trump ally Elon Musk is using social media to prime voter mistrust ahead of 2024 election |publisher=CBS News |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/elon-musk-trump-social-media-election-2024/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241109015540/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/elon-musk-trump-social-media-election-2024/ |archive-date=November 9, 2024 |access-date=October 22, 2024 |language=en-US}}</ref> Musk was the largest individual donor of the 2024 election.<ref name="Thadani 12062024">{{Cite news |last1=Thadani |first1=Trisha |last2=Morse |first2=Clara Ence |date=December 6, 2024 |title=Elon Musk is now America's largest political donor |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2024/12/06/elon-musk-trump-campaign-spending-fec/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250101000528/https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2024/12/06/elon-musk-trump-campaign-spending-fec/ |archive-date=January 1, 2025 |access-date=December 31, 2024 |newspaper=The Washington Post |language=en |issn=0190-8286}}</ref> In 2025, Musk contributed $19 million to the [[2025 Wisconsin Supreme Court election|Wisconsin Supreme Court race]], hoping to influence the state's future [[redistricting]] efforts and its regulations governing car manufacturers and dealers.<ref>{{cite web |last=Schulz |first=Joe |date=March 3, 2025 |title=As Musk pours millions into Wisconsin Supreme Court race, Tesla files case that could reach justices |url=https://www.wpr.org/news/elon-musk-pac-millions-wisconsin-supreme-court-race-tesla-lawsuit |website=Wisconsin Public Radio |access-date=March 26, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Walker |first=Chris |date=March 26, 2025 |title=Musk Pours Millions Into Wisconsin Court Race to Protect Rigged Maps for GOP |url=https://truthout.org/articles/musk-pours-millions-into-wisconsin-court-race-to-protect-rigged-maps-for-gop/ |website=Truthout |access-date=March 26, 2025 |archive-date=March 26, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250326185047/https://truthout.org/articles/musk-pours-millions-into-wisconsin-court-race-to-protect-rigged-maps-for-gop/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

Musk's international political actions and comments have come under increasing scrutiny and criticism, especially from the governments and leaders of France, Germany, Norway, Spain and the United Kingdom, particularly due to his position in the [[Second Trump administration|U.S. government]] as well as ownership of X.<ref name="Times">{{Cite news |last=Times |first=The Brussels |title=Musk-AfD: EU Commission to monitor risks of 'preferential treatment' |url=https://www.brusselstimes.com/1380216/musk-afd-debate-eu-commission-to-monitor-risks-of-preferential-treatment |access-date=January 7, 2025 |website=Brussels Times |language=en}}</ref><ref name="European">{{multiref2|{{Cite news |last=Henley |first=Jon |date=January 6, 2025 |title=Emmanuel Macron joins growing criticism of Elon Musk in Europe |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jan/06/emmanuel-macron-joins-growing-criticism-elon-musk-europe |access-date=January 7, 2025 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}|{{Cite web |last=Hutchison |first=Peter |title=European leaders in France, Norway and Germany hit back against Elon Musk in UK political meddling row |agency=[[Agence France-Presse]] |url=https://fortune.com/europe/2025/01/06/european-leaders-france-norway-germany-hit-back-against-elon-musk-political-meddling/ |access-date=January 7, 2025 |website=Fortune Europe |language=en |archive-date=January 7, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250107032200/https://fortune.com/europe/2025/01/06/european-leaders-france-norway-germany-hit-back-against-elon-musk-political-meddling/ |url-status=live}}|{{Cite news |title=European leaders decry Elon Musk's meddling |date=January 6, 2025 |url=https://www.dw.com/en/european-leaders-decry-elon-musks-meddling/a-71227690 |access-date=January 7, 2025 |publisher=Deutsche Welle |language=en |archive-date=January 7, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250107032159/https://www.dw.com/en/european-leaders-decry-elon-musks-meddling/a-71227690 |url-status=live}}|{{Cite news |date=January 6, 2025 |title=Elon Musk's European political meddling is 'worrying,' says Norway's PM|author-first1=Ketrin|author-last1=Jochecová|url=https://www.politico.eu/article/norwegian-pm-jonas-gahr-store-worried-elon-musk-political-meddling/ |access-date=January 7, 2025 |website=Politico |language=en-GB |archive-date=January 6, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250106163545/https://www.politico.eu/article/norwegian-pm-jonas-gahr-store-worried-elon-musk-political-meddling/ |url-status=live}}|{{Cite news |date=January 7, 2025 |title=Musk provokes European leaders ahead of chat with German far-right leader |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crmngpvv08lo.amp |access-date=January 8, 2025 |publisher=[[BBC News]] |language=en-gb |archive-date=January 8, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250108060720/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crmngpvv08lo.amp |url-status=live}}
}}</ref><ref name="AfD">{{multiref2|{{Cite news |last=Dorn |first=Sara |title=Foreign Leaders—And The EU—Step Up Challenges To Musk As His Feuds With Global Politicians Heat Up |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn/2025/01/06/foreign-leaders-and-the-eu-step-up-challenges-to-musk-as-his-feuds-with-global-politicians-heat-up/ |access-date=January 7, 2025 |website=Forbes |language=en |archive-date=January 6, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250106211020/https://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn/2025/01/06/foreign-leaders-and-the-eu-step-up-challenges-to-musk-as-his-feuds-with-global-politicians-heat-up/ |url-status=live}}|{{Cite news |last=Tankersley |first=Jim |date=January 9, 2025 |title=Elon Musk Is Trying to Break Germany's Quarantine on the Far-Right AfD |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/09/world/europe/germany-elon-musk-afd.html |access-date=February 2, 2025 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331 |archive-date=January 28, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250128171121/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/09/world/europe/germany-elon-musk-afd.html |url-status=live}}|{{Cite news |last=Psaropoulos |first=John T. |title=Is Elon Musk a Nazi, and can he get European far-right hardliners elected? |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/1/31/is-elon-musk-a-nazi-and-can-he-get-european-far-right-hardliners-elected |access-date=February 2, 2025 |publisher=Al Jazeera English |language=en}}|{{Cite news |last=Ewing |first=Giselle Ruhiyyih |date=January 25, 2025 |title=Musk tells Germans to get over 'past guilt' in speech to far-right AfD rally |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2025/01/25/musk-german-afd-rally-weidel-00200620 |access-date=February 2, 2025 |website=Politico |language=en |archive-date=January 27, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250127141630/https://www.politico.com/news/2025/01/25/musk-german-afd-rally-weidel-00200620 |url-status=live}}
