al Center]]}}</ref><ref name=":9">{{Cite web |date=January 23, 2025 |title=Elon Musk makes Holocaust jokes after Netanyahu defends him as 'great friend of Israel' |url=https://www.jpost.com/diaspora/article-839006 |access-date=April 22, 2025 |website=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":02">{{Cite web |last=Pengelly |first=Martin |date=January 26, 2025 |title=Jewish non-profit chief says Musk will spur violence with his 'Nazi salute' |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jan/26/elon-musk-far-right-antisemitism |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250130062917/https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jan/26/elon-musk-far-right-antisemitism |archive-date=January 30, 2025 |access-date=January 29, 2025 |website=[[The Guardian]] |issn=1756-3224 |oclc=60623878}}</ref> American public opinion was divided on partisan lines as to whether it was a fascist salute.<ref name=":10">{{Cite web |date=February 1, 2025 |title=YouGov Survey: Elon Musk's Gesture |url=https://d3nkl3psvxxpe9.cloudfront.net/documents/Elon_Musk_Gesture_poll_results.pdf |access-date=April 14, 2025 |website=[[YouGov]]}}</ref> Musk dismissed the accusations of [[Nazi]] sympathies, deriding them as "dirty tricks" and a "tired" attack.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wickman |first=Kase |date=January 21, 2025 |title=Elon Musk Sure Isn't Denying That His Inaugural Gesture Was a Nazi Salute |url=https://www.vanityfair.com/style/story/elon-musk-inauguration-gesture-nazi-salute |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250130160537/https://www.vanityfair.com/style/story/elon-musk-inauguration-gesture-nazi-salute |archive-date=January 30, 2025 |access-date=February 6, 2025 |website=[[Vanity Fair (magazine)|Vanity Fair]] |publisher=[[Condé Nast]] |language=en-US |issn=0733-8899 |oclc=8356733}}</ref><ref name="Fortinsky-2025a">{{Cite news |last=Fortinsky |first=Sarah |date=January 21, 2025 |title=Musk on salute blowback: 'Frankly, they need better dirty tricks' |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/5097672-elon-musk-responds-salute-criticism/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250130130909/https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/5097672-elon-musk-responds-salute-criticism/ |archive-date=January 30, 2025 |access-date=February 6, 2025 |website=[[The Hill (newspaper)|The Hill]] |publisher=[[Nexstar Media Group]] |issn=1521-1568 |oclc=31153202}}</ref> [[Neo-Nazi]] and [[white supremacist]] groups celebrated it as a Nazi salute.<ref name="Condon-2025">{{Cite news |last=Condon |first=Bernard |date=January 22, 2025 |title=Musk's straight-arm gesture embraced by right-wing extremists regardless of what he meant |url=https://apnews.com/article/musk-gesture-salute-antisemitism-0070dae53c7a73397b104ae645877535 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250130185508/https://apnews.com/article/musk-gesture-salute-antisemitism-0070dae53c7a73397b104ae645877535 |archive-date=January 30, 2025 |access-date=February 6, 2025 |work=[[Associated Press]]}}</ref><ref name=":12" /> Multiple European political parties demanded that Musk be banned from entering their countries.<ref>{{cite web |last=Strauß |first=Hagen |date=January 22, 2025 |title='Unterstützer der extremen Rechten': Linke will Einreisesperre für Elon Musk |trans-title='Supporter of the Extreme Right': Die Linke calls for Entry Ban for Elon Musk |url=https://rp-online.de/politik/deutschland/elon-musk-linke-will-einreiseverbot-fuer-trump-berater_aid-123327325 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250123062821/https://rp-online.de/politik/deutschland/elon-musk-linke-will-einreiseverbot-fuer-trump-berater_aid-123327325 |archive-date=January 23, 2025 |access-date=January 22, 2025 |work=[[Rheinische Post]] |language=de}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=January 21, 2025 |title=Österreichs Grüne fordern Einreiseverbot für Elon Musk |trans-title=Austria's Greens Demand Entry Ban for Elon Musk |url=https://kurier.at/politik/ausland/elon-musk-donald-trump-einreiseverbot-oesterreich/403001192 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250130023523/https://kurier.at/politik/ausland/elon-musk-donald-trump-einreiseverbot-oesterreich/403001192 |archive-date=January 30, 2025 |access-date=January 22, 2025 |work=[[Kurier]] |language=de |issn=2308-0973 |oclc=849575488}}</ref>

=== Department of Government Efficiency ===
{{Main|Department of Government Efficiency}}
[[File:Elon Musk (54350004520).jpg|thumb|left|150px|Elon Musk wielding a chainsaw at the [[Conservative Political Action Conference]] (CPAC) in 2025, imitating a publicity stunt used by [[Javier Milei]] symbolic of efficiency, [[2025 United States federal mass layoffs|federal mass layoffs]] and [[tax cut]]ting]]

The concept of DOGE emerged in a discussion between Musk and [[Donald Trump]], and in August 2024, Trump committed to giving Musk an advisory role, with Musk accepting the offer.<ref name="Shepardson">{{Cite news |last=Shepardson |first=David |date=August 20, 2024 |title=Trump says he may end EV tax credit; is open to naming Elon Musk as an adviser |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-says-he-would-consider-ending-7500-electric-vehicle-credit-2024-08-19/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241206064735/https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-says-he-would-consider-ending-7500-electric-vehicle-credit-2024-08-19/ |archive-date=December 6, 2024 |access-date=November 13, 2024 |publisher=Reuters}}</ref> In November and December 2024, Musk suggested that the organization could help to cut the [[United States federal budget|U.S. federal budget]], consolidate the number of federal agencies,<ref>{{Cite news |last=Picchi |first=Aimee |date=November 14, 2024 |title=What to know about Trump's Department of Government Efficiency, led by Elon Musk and Vivek Ramaswamy - CBS News |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-department-of-government-efficiency-doge-elon-musk-ramaswamy/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241117233859/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-department-of-government-efficiency-doge-elon-musk-ramaswamy/ |archive-date=November 17, 2024 |access-date=November 18, 2024 |publisher=CBS News |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Jones |first=Ja'han |date=November 13, 2024 |title=Trump's meme-ified 'efficiency' 'department' is equal parts cockamamie and conflict |url=https://www.msnbc.com/the-reidout/reidout-blog/department-government-efficiency-doge-gift-vivek-ramaswamy-elon-musk-rcna179976 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241117155653/https://www.msnbc.com/the-reidout/reidout-blog/department-government-efficiency-doge-gift-vivek-ramaswamy-elon-musk-rcna179976 |archive-date=November 17, 2024 |access-date=November 18, 2024 |publisher=MSNBC |language=en}}</ref> and eliminate the [[Consumer Financial Protection Bureau]],<ref>{{Cite news |date=November 27, 2024 |title=Elon Musk wants to 'delete' federal financial watchdog as 'DOGE' begins work |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/11/27/elon-musk-delete-cfpb-doge/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241127191821/https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/11/27/elon-musk-delete-cfpb-doge/ |archive-date=November 27, 2024 |access-date=November 27, 2024 |newspaper=The Washington Post}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=November 27, 2024 |title=Musk calls for abolishing consumer finance watchdog targeted by Republicans |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us/musk-calls-abolishing-consumer-finance-watchdog-targeted-by-republicans-2024-11-27/ |publisher=Reuters}}</ref> and that its final stage would be "deleting itself".<ref>{{Cite news |last=Siddiqui |first=Faiz |date=December 21, 2024 |title=Elon Musk's wish list for DOGE |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/12/20/elon-musk-doge-priorities/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241222082229/https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/12/20/elon-musk-doge-priorities/ |archive-date=December 22, 2024 |access-date=February 8, 2025 |newspaper=[[The Washington Post]]}}</ref>

In January 2025, the organization was created by [[executive order]], and Musk was designated a "[[special government employee]]".<ref name="MD2">{{Cite news |last=Ingram |first=David |date=February 4, 2025 |title=Elon Musk and DOGE are hacking the government |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/elon-musk-doge-usaid-treasury-government-rcna190450 |access-date=February 4, 2025 |publisher=NBC News |language=en |archive-date=February 4, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250204120250/https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/elon-musk-doge-usaid-treasury-government-rcna190450 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="Ngo 1212025">{{Cite news |last1=Madeline |first1=Ngo |last2=Schleifer |first2=Theodore |date=January 21, 2025 |title=How Trump's Department of Government Efficiency Will Work |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/21/us/politics/doge-government-efficiency-trump-musk.html |url-access=subscription |access-date=January 21, 2025 |work=The New York Times |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Musk is leading the organization and is a [[Senior Advisor to the President of the United States|senior advisor to the president]],<ref>{{Cite news |date=February 18, 2025 |title=Musk is just an adviser with no power to make decisions, White House claims |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/18/turmp-elon-musk-doge |access-date=March 13, 2025 |work=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref> although his [[Political activities of Elon Musk|official role]] is not clear.<ref name="Wolf2">{{Cite news |last=Wolf |first=Zachary B. |date=February 1, 2025 |title=Analysis: We do not know what exactly Elon Musk is doing to the federal government {{!}} CNN Politics |url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/02/01/politics/elon-musk-federal-government-what-matters/index.html |access-date=February 1, 2025 |publisher=[[CNN]] |language=en |archive-date=February 5, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250205062842/https://www.cnn.com/2025/02/01/politics/elon-musk-federal-government-what-matters/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref> In sworn statement during a lawsuit, the director of the White House [[Office of Administration]] stated that Musk "is not an employee of the U.S. DOGE Service or U.S. DOGE Service Temporary Organization", "is not the U.S. DOGE Service administrator", and has "no actual or formal authority to make government decisions himself".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Quinn |first=Melissa |date=February 18, 2025 |title=Judge won't block Musk and DOGE from accessing data, making cuts at 7 federal agencies |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/judge-wont-block-musks-doge-from-accessing-data-making-cuts-at-7-federal-agencies/ |access-date=February 19, 2025 |website=CBS News |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Bortos |first1=Alena |title=Elon Musk isn't in charge of DOGE or even an employee of it, White House says |url=https://fortune.com/2025/02/18/elon-musk-doge-head-employee/ |access-date=February 20, 2025 |work=Fortune |date=February 18, 2025 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250218213906/https://fortune.com/2025/02/18/elon-musk-doge-head-employee/ |archive-date=February 18, 2025}}</ref> Trump said two days later that he had put Musk in charge of DOGE.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Shalal |first1=Andrea |last2=Bose |first2=Nandita |title=Trump appears to contradict White House, says Elon Musk in charge of DOGE |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-appears-contradict-white-house-says-elon-musk-charge-doge-2025-02-20/ |access-date=February 20, 2025 |work=Reuters |date=February 20, 2025}}</ref> A federal judge has ruled that Musk acts as the ''de facto'' leader of DOGE.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Lee |first1=Ella |title=Judge finds Elon Musk likely acted unconstitutionally in shuttering USAID |url=https://thehill.com/regulation/court-battles/5201430-judge-elon-musk-usaid/ |access-date=March 18, 2025 |work=[[The Hill (newspaper)|The Hill]] |date=March 18, 2025 |quote=It marks the first time a judge has ruled that Musk is likely exercising enough independent authority to require him to be confirmed by the Senate under the Constitution's Appointments Clause. "The record of his activities to date establishes that his role has been and will continue to be as the leader of DOGE, with the same duties and degree of continuity as if he was formally in that position,'" wrote Chuang, an appointee of former President Obama. Chuang rejected the Trump administration's argument that Musk is not the DOGE administrator and is instead merely a senior adviser to the president who has no independent authority.}}</ref>

[[File:President Trump Participates in a Press Conference with Elon Musk.webm|thumb|Elon Musk participating in a press conference with Donald Trump shortly before his departure from DOGE]]

Musk's role in the [[second Trump administration]], particularly in [[Response to the Department of Government Efficiency|response to DOGE]], has [[Protests against Elon Musk|attracted public backlash]]. He was criticized for his treatment of federal government employees,<ref name="nyt-young-aides-25">{{cite news |last1=Schleifer |first1=Theodore |last2=Nehamas |first2=Nicholas |last3=Conger |first3=Kate |last4=Mac |first4=Ryan |date=February 7, 2025 |title=Young Aides Emerge as Enforcers in Musk's Broadside Against Government |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/07/us/politics/musk-doge-aides.html |access-date=February 7, 2025 |work=[[The New York Times]] |archive-date=February 8, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250208014401/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/07/us/politics/musk-doge-aides.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="nyt-swan-musk-feb-25">{{cite news |last1=Swan |first1=Jonathan |last2=Schleifer |first2=Theodore |last3=Haberman |first3=Maggie |last4=Conger |first4=Kate |last5=Mac |first5=Ryan |last6=Ngo |first6=Madeleine |date=February 3, 2025 |title=Inside Musk's Aggressive Incursion Into the Federal Government |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/03/us/politics/musk-federal-government.html |access-date=February 4, 2025 |work=[[The New York Times]] |archive-date=February 7, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250207132659/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/03/us/politics/musk-federal-government.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="wp-zs-25">{{cite news |last1=Zakrzewski |first1=Cat |last2=Siddiqui |first2=Faiz |date=February 5, 2025 |title=How Elon Musk's deputies took over the government's most basic functions |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2025/02/05/elon-musk-federal-technology-takeover/ |access-date=February 5, 2025 |newspaper=[[The Washington Post]] |archive-date=February 6, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250206221232/https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2025/02/05/elon-musk-federal-technology-takeover/ |url-status=live }}</ref> including his influence over the [[2025 United States federal mass layoffs|mass layoffs of the federal workforce]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Neely |first1=Brett |last2=Bowman |first2=Emma |title=Elon Musk tells federal employees to document work in email or be fired |url=https://www.npr.org/2025/02/22/nx-s1-5305834/elon-musk-federal-employees-email-opm |access-date=February 23, 2025 |work=NPR |date=February 22, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Volcovici |first1=Valerie |title=Musk orders US federal workers to report on work by Monday or resign |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us/musk-orders-us-federal-workers-report-work-or-get-fired-2025-02-22/ |access-date=February 23, 2025 |work=Reuters |date=February 23, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Fortinsky |first1=Sarah |title=Musk says failure to respond a second time to email will end in termination |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/5162218-musk-says-failure-to-respond-a-second-time-to-email-will-end-in-termination/ |access-date=February 26, 2025 |work=The Hill |date=February 24, 2025}}</ref> He has prioritized secrecy within the organization<ref name="The New York Times">{{cite news |last1=Swan |first1=Jonathan |last2=Schleifer |first2=Theodore |last3=Haberman |first3=Maggie |last4=Conger |first4=Kate |last5=Mac |first5=Ryan |last6=Ngo |first6=Madeleine |date=February 3, 2025 |title=Inside Musk's Aggressive Incursion Into the Federal Government |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/03/us/politics/musk-federal-government.html?unlocked_article_code=1.uU4.HQRZ.uQoWMVaZtOnr&smid=url-share |work=The New York Times}}</ref> and has accused others of violating privacy laws.<ref name="MD2"/> A Senate report alleged that Musk could avoid up to $2 billion in legal liability as a result of DOGE's actions.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Nazzaro |first=Miranda |date=April 28, 2025 |title=Musk, companies could avoid $2 billion in potential liability over DOGE role: Report |url=https://thehill.com/policy/technology/5271301-elon-musk-government-liability/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250429044224/https://thehill.com/policy/technology/5271301-elon-musk-government-liability/ |archive-date=April 29, 2025 |access-date=May 9, 2025 |work=The Hill |language=en-US |url-status=live }}</ref> In May 2025, [[Bill Gates]] accused Musk of "killing the world's poorest children" through his cuts to [[United States Agency for International Development|USAID]],<ref>{{Cite news |last=Pilling |first=David |date=May 8, 2025 |title=Bill Gates accuses Elon Musk of 'killing' children with USAID cuts |url=https://www.ft.com/content/bdd9bb89-ac3c-4043-9ca4-bc7efbd41fed |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250509190635/https://www.ft.com/content/bdd9bb89-ac3c-4043-9ca4-bc7efbd41fed |archive-date=May 9, 2025 |access-date=May 15, 2025 |work=Financial Times}}</ref> which modeling by [[Boston University]] estimated had resulted in 300,000 deaths by this time, most of them of children.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Goldberg |first=Michelle |date=May 30, 2025 |title=Elon Musk's Legacy Is Disease, Starvation and Death |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/30/opinion/elon-musk-doge-usaid.html |access-date=May 30, 2025 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Emanuel |first1=Gabrielle |last2=Inskeep |first2=Steve |date=May 28, 2025 |title=Aid groups say USAID cuts are already having deadly consequences |url=https://www.npr.org/2025/05/28/nx-s1-5413322/aid-groups-say-usaid-cuts-are-already-having-deadly-consequences |access-date=May 20, 2025 |publisher=NPR}}</ref>

Musk announced on May 28, 2025, that he would depart from the Trump administration as planned when the special government employee's 130 day deadline expired,<ref>{{cite news|url=https://apnews.com/article/elon-musk-donald-trump-big-beautiful-bill-aa2bc70b0ebdb219b5dd3e9f8fae03af|title=Elon Musk is leaving the Trump administration after criticizing president's 'big beautiful bill'|first1=Chris|last1=Megerian|first2=Kevin|last2=Freking|publisher=Associated Press|date=May 28, 2025|accessdate=May 28, 2025}}</ref> with a White House official confirming that Musk's [[Employee offboarding|offboarding]] from the Trump administration was already underway.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us/elon-musk-leaving-trump-administration-white-house-official-confirms-2025-05-29/|title=Elon Musk leaving Trump administration, White House official confirms|first1=Nandita|last1=Bose|first2=David|last2=Shepardson|publisher=Reuters|date=May 28, 2025|accessdate=May 28, 2025}}</ref> His departure was officially confirmed during a joint Oval Office press conference with Trump on May 30, 2025.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://people.com/elon-musk-donald-trump-final-joint-press-conference-11745206|title=Donald Trump and Elon Musk Come Face to Face in Oval Office Hours After Bombshell Report About Musk's 'Intense' Drug Use|first=Meredith|last=Kile|publisher=People|date=May 30, 2025|accessdate=May 30, 2025}}</ref>

