After leaving office, Musk criticized the Trump administration's [[One Big Beautiful Bill Act|Big Beautiful Bill]], calling it a "disgusting abomination" due to its provisions increasing the deficit.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Conger |first1=Kate |last2=Gold |first2=Michael |last3=Swan |first3=Jonathan |date=June 3, 2025 |title=Elon Musk Calls Trump Policy Bill a 'Disgusting Abomination' |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/03/technology/elon-musk-criticizes-republican-legislation.html |access-date=June 4, 2025 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> A feud began between Musk and Trump, with its most notable event being Musk alleging Trump had ties to sex offender [[Jeffrey Epstein]] on X (formerly Twitter) on June 5, 2025.<ref name="Epstein1">{{cite web |title=Trump and Musk escalate public feud over agenda bill |url=https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/trump-president-administration-news-06-05-25 |website=cnn.com |date=June 5, 2025 |publisher=CNN |access-date=June 5, 2025}}</ref><ref name="Epstein2">{{cite web |title=Live Updates: Trump and Elon Musk Spar Over Domestic Policy Bill as Relationship Frays |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2025/06/05/us/trump-elon-musk |website=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=June 5, 2025 |last1=Pager |first1=Tyler |last2=Schleifer |first2=Theodore |date=June 5, 2025 }}</ref> Trump responded on [[Truth Social]] stating that Musk went "CRAZY" after the "EV Mandate" was purportedly taken away and threatened to cut Musk's government contracts.{{Sfn|Pager|2025d}}{{Sfn|Pager|2025e}} Musk then called for a third Trump impeachment.{{Sfn|Basu|2025}} The next day, Trump stated that he did not wish to reconcile with Musk, and added that Musk would face "very serious consequences" if he funds Democratic candidates.{{Sfn|Welker|Marquez|2025}} On June 11, Musk publicly apologized for the tweets against Trump, saying they "went too far."<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Martínez |first1=Andrés R. |last2=Satariano |first2=Adam |date=June 11, 2025 |title=Elon Musk Says His Trump Criticisms 'Went Too Far' |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/11/business/elon-musk-trump-feud.html |access-date=June 11, 2025 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

