022/12/elon-musk-twitter-far-right-activist/672436/ |access-date=July 31, 2024 |website=[[The Atlantic]] |language=en |archive-date=December 12, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221212052001/https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2022/12/elon-musk-twitter-far-right-activist/672436/ |url-status=live |ref=none}}|4={{Cite news |last=Conroy |first=J. Oliver |date=January 4, 2025 |title=How Elon Musk's X became the global right's supercharged front page |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jan/04/elon-musk-x-trump-far-right |access-date=February 6, 2025 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077 |ref=none}}}}</ref> His views have been characterized as [[Libertarianism in the United States|libertarian]] and [[far-right]],<ref name="Libertarian">{{multiref2|{{Cite news |last=Foroohar |first=Rana |date=November 25, 2024 |title=Elon Musk's vision for a libertarian utopia |url=https://www.ft.com/content/bb70a07e-0da6-4faf-b69e-fb47ca27ac43 |access-date=February 7, 2025 |work=[[Financial Times]] |ref=none}}|{{Cite web |last=Maher |first=Henry |date=January 26, 2025 |title=Elon Musk now has an office in the White House. What's his political game plan? |url=https://theconversation.com/elon-musk-now-has-an-office-in-the-white-house-whats-his-political-game-plan-248011 |access-date=February 7, 2025 |website=[[The Conversation (website)|The Conversation]] |language=en-US |archive-date=January 30, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250130160632/https://theconversation.com/elon-musk-now-has-an-office-in-the-white-house-whats-his-political-game-plan-248011 |url-status=live |ref=none}}|{{Cite web |last=Davies |first=Pascale |date=October 30, 2024 |title='Techno libertarians': Why Elon Musk is supporting Donald Trump in the US election |url=https://www.euronews.com/next/2024/10/30/techno-libertarians-why-elon-musk-is-supporting-donald-trump-in-the-us-election |access-date=February 7, 2025 |website=[[Euronews]] |ref=none}}|{{Cite web |last1=Amlinger |first1=Carolin |last2=Nachtwey |first2=Oliver |date=January 29, 2025 |title=In Elon Musk, Libertarianism and Authoritarianism Combine |url=https://jacobin.com/2025/01/musk-authoritarianism-libertarianism-afd-trump |access-date=February 7, 2025 |website=[[Jacobin]] |language=en-US |archive-date=January 30, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250130040002/https://jacobin.com/2025/01/musk-authoritarianism-libertarianism-afd-trump/ |url-status=live |ref=none}}
}}</ref><ref name="Far-right">{{multiref2|1={{Cite magazine |last=Gilbert |first=David |date=February 5, 2025 |title=The Far Right Has a New Hero: Elon Musk |url=https://www.wired.com/story/far-right-new-leader-elon-musk/ |access-date=February 6, 2025 |magazine=[[Wired (magazine)|Wired]] |language=en-US |issn=1059-1028 |ref=none}}|2={{Cite web |last=Fitzpatrick |first=Matt |date=February 1, 2025 |title=The far-right is rising at a crucial time in Germany, boosted by Elon Musk |url=https://theconversation.com/the-far-right-is-rising-at-a-crucial-time-in-germany-boosted-by-elon-musk-247895 |access-date=February 6, 2025 |website=[[The Conversation (website)|The Conversation]] |language=en-US |ref=none}}|3={{Cite news |last=Nietfeld |first=Kay |date=January 10, 2025 |title=Musk doubles down on support for German far-right leader |url=https://www.lemonde.fr/en/europe/article/2025/01/10/musk-doubles-down-on-support-for-german-far-right-leader_6736883_143.html |access-date=February 6, 2025 |work=[[Le Monde]] |language=en |ref=none}}|4={{Cite web |last=Psaropoulos |first=John T. |date=January 31, 2025 |title=Is Elon Musk a Nazi, and can he get European far-right hardliners elected? |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/1/31/is-elon-musk-a-nazi-and-can-he-get-european-far-right-hardliners-elected |access-date=February 6, 2025 |publisher=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en |ref=none}}}}</ref> and after his [[Political activities of Elon Musk|involvement in European politics]], they have received criticism from world leaders such as [[Emmanuel Macron]] and [[Olaf Scholz]].<ref name="olaf">{{Cite web |last1=Starcevic |first1=Seb |last2=Sahlberg |first2=Johanna |date=January 17, 2025 |title=Scholz: Elon Musk is a danger to European democracy |url=https://www.politico.eu/article/olaf-scholz-elon-musk-is-a-danger-to-european-democracy/ |access-date=June 7, 2025 |website=POLITICO}}</ref><ref name="Henley-2025">{{multiref2|{{Cite news |last=Henley |first=Jon |date=January 6, 2025 |title=Emmanuel Macron joins growing criticism of Elon Musk in Europe |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jan/06/emmanuel-macron-joins-growing-criticism-elon-musk-europe |access-date=January 7, 2025 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077 |ref=none}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hutchison,AFP |first=Peter |date=January 6, 2025 |title=European leaders in France, Norway and Germany hit back against Elon Musk in UK political meddling row |url=https://fortune.com/europe/2025/01/06/european-leaders-france-norway-germany-hit-back-against-elon-musk-political-meddling/ |access-date=January 7, 2025 |website=[[Fortune (magazine)|Fortune]] |language=en |archive-date=January 7, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250107032200/https://fortune.com/europe/2025/01/06/european-leaders-france-norway-germany-hit-back-against-elon-musk-political-meddling/ |url-status=live |ref=none}}|{{Cite web |date=January 6, 2025 |title=European leaders decry Elon Musk's meddling |url=https://www.dw.com/en/european-leaders-decry-elon-musks-meddling/a-71227690 |access-date=January 7, 2025 |publisher=[[Deutsche Welle]] |language=en |archive-date=January 7, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250107032159/https://www.dw.com/en/european-leaders-decry-elon-musks-meddling/a-71227690 |url-status=live |ref=none}}|{{Cite web |first=Ketrin |last=Jochecová |date=January 6, 2025 |title=Elon Musk's European political meddling is 'worrying,' says Norway's PM |url=https://www.politico.eu/article/norwegian-pm-jonas-gahr-store-worried-elon-musk-political-meddling/ |access-date=January 7, 2025 |website=[[Politico]] |language=en-GB |archive-date=January 6, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250106163545/https://www.politico.eu/article/norwegian-pm-jonas-gahr-store-worried-elon-musk-political-meddling/ |url-status=live |ref=none}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |first1=Paul |last1=Kirby |first2=Laura |last2=Gozzi |date=January 7, 2025 |title=Musk provokes European leaders ahead of chat with German far-right leader |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crmngpvv08lo.amp |access-date=January 8, 2025 |publisher=[[BBC News]] |language=en-gb |archive-date=January 8, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250108060720/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crmngpvv08lo.amp |url-status=live |ref=none}}
}}</ref>

Within the context of [[Views of Elon Musk#U.S. politics|American politics]], Musk supported Democratic candidates up until 2022, at which point he voted for a Republican for the first time.<ref name=":0" /><ref name=":2" /><ref name=":1" /> He has stated support for [[universal basic income]],<ref name="uni2">{{cite news |last=Strange |first=Adario |date=November 5, 2016 |title=Elon Musk thinks universal income is answer to automation taking human jobs |url=http://mashable.com/2016/11/05/elon-musk-universal-basic-income/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200901223023/https://mashable.com/2016/11/05/elon-musk-universal-basic-income/ |archive-date=September 1, 2020 |access-date=February 6, 2017 |website=[[mashable.com]]}}</ref> [[gun rights]],<ref>{{Cite news |date=May 26, 2022 |title=Elon Musk risks MAGA ire by calling for gun control |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/elon-musk-gun-control-texas-b2088098.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220527201600/https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/elon-musk-gun-control-texas-b2088098.html |archive-date=May 27, 2022 |access-date=June 13, 2022 |website=The Independent |language=en}}</ref> [[freedom of speech]],<ref>{{Cite news |last=Stimson |first=Brie |date=March 5, 2022 |title=Elon Musk says Starlink won't block Russian state media in Ukraine: 'Sorry to be a free speech absolutist' |url=https://www.foxbusiness.com/business-leaders/elon-musk-starlink-russian-state-media-ukraine-free-speech-absolutist |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220313171346/https://www.foxbusiness.com/business-leaders/elon-musk-starlink-russian-state-media-ukraine-free-speech-absolutist |archive-date=March 13, 2022 |access-date=June 13, 2022 |publisher=Fox Business |language=en-US}}</ref> a [[tax on carbon emissions]],<ref>{{cite news |last1=Birnbaum |first1=Emily |date=December 13, 2021 |title=Musk spurns subsidies, after SpaceX sought them out |url=https://www.politico.com/newsletters/morning-tech/2021/12/13/musk-spurns-subsidies-after-spacex-sought-them-out-799430 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220525134347/https://www.politico.com/newsletters/morning-tech/2021/12/13/musk-spurns-subsidies-after-spacex-sought-them-out-799430 |archive-date=May 25, 2022 |access-date=May 25, 2022 |work=Politico |language=en}}</ref> and [[H-1B visa]]s.<ref name="CBS News-2024">{{Cite news |date=December 27, 2024 |title=Musk and Ramaswamy are sparking a debate over the H-1B visa. Here's what to know about the visa |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/musk-vivek-ramaswamy-h1b-visa-maga-immigration-what-to-know/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241227225338/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/musk-vivek-ramaswamy-h1b-visa-maga-immigration-what-to-know/ |archive-date=December 27, 2024 |access-date=December 28, 2024 |publisher=CBS News |language=en-US}}</ref> Musk has expressed concern about issues such as [[artificial intelligence]] (AI)<ref name="wp2015">{{cite news |last=Fung |first=Brian |date=July 28, 2015 |title=Elon Musk and Stephen Hawking think we should ban killer robots |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/the-switch/wp/2015/07/28/elon-musk-and-stephen-hawking-think-we-should-ban-killer-robots/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160308074506/http://www.washingtonpost.com/news/the-switch/wp/2015/07/28/elon-musk-and-stephen-hawking-think-we-should-ban-killer-robots/ |archive-date=March 8, 2016 |access-date=January 5, 2017 |newspaper=The Washington Post}}</ref> and [[climate change]],<ref>{{cite news |title=US quits Paris climate pact: Reaction from around the world following the US president's decision on the Paris accord |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/world-us-canada-40123293 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170829015328/http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/world-us-canada-40123293 |archive-date=August 29, 2017 |access-date=June 1, 2017}}</ref> and has been a critic of [[wealth tax]],<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Levin |first1=Tim |last2=Mitchell |first2=Taiyler S. |date=December 7, 2021 |title=Elon Musk says he supports a controversial tax that many of his billionaire peers despise |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-estate-tax-billionaires-wealth-2021-12 |access-date=December 31, 2024 |work=Business Insider}}</ref> [[short-selling]],<ref>{{Cite news |last=Mohamed |first=Theron |title='Short selling should be illegal' – Elon Musk praised a crackdown on shorts by the world's biggest pension fund |url=https://markets.businessinsider.com/news/stocks/tesla-spacex-ceo-elon-musk-short-selling-should-be-illegal-2019-12-1028733903 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200807084710/https://markets.businessinsider.com/news/stocks/tesla-spacex-ceo-elon-musk-short-selling-should-be-illegal-2019-12-1028733903 |archive-date=August 7, 2020 |access-date=June 14, 2020 |work=Business Insider |language=en-us}}</ref> and [[government subsidies]].<ref>{{cite news |date=December 7, 2021 |title=Elon Musk doubles down on ending 'subsidies' as competitors now reap more benefits |url=https://www.cnn.com/2021/12/07/tech/elon-musk-wsj-government/index.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230330154400/https://www.cnn.com/2021/12/07/tech/elon-musk-wsj-government/index.html |archive-date=March 30, 2023 |access-date=April 1, 2023 |publisher=[[CNN]] }}</ref> An immigrant himself, Musk has been accused of being [[anti-immigration]], and regularly blames [[Immigration policy of the United States|immigration policies]] for [[Illegal immigration to the United States|illegal immigration]].<ref name="Fearmongering">{{Cite news |date=March 5, 2024 |title=Elon Musk can't stop fearmongering on immigration |url=https://www.msnbc.com/top-stories/latest/elon-musk-conspiracy-theory-immigration-terror-rcna141827 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240312184020/https://www.msnbc.com/top-stories/latest/elon-musk-conspiracy-theory-immigration-terror-rcna141827 |archive-date=March 12, 2024 |access-date=March 12, 2024 |publisher=MSNBC |language=en}}</ref> He is also a [[pronatalist]] who believes [[population decline]] is the biggest threat to civilization,<ref name="Pronatlist">{{multiref2|1={{cite news |last1=Dodds |first1=Io |date=April 17, 2023 |title=Meet the 'elite' couples breeding to save mankind |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/family/life/pronatalists-save-mankind-by-having-babies-silicon-valley/ |access-date=October 13, 2024 |newspaper=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |ref=none}}|2={{cite news |last1=Kleeman |first1=Jenny |date=May 25, 2024 |title=The world's most famous pronatalist |url=https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/article/2024/may/25/american-pronatalists-malcolm-and-simone-collins |access-date=October 13, 2024 |website=[[The Guardian]] |ref=none}}|3={{cite news |date=December 7, 2021 |title=Elon Musk says there aren't 'enough people,' birthrate could threaten human civilization |url=https://eu.usatoday.com/story/money/business/2021/12/07/elon-musk-declining-birthrate-threatens-human-civilization/6414749001/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220510142824/https://eu.usatoday.com/story/money/business/2021/12/07/elon-musk-declining-birthrate-threatens-human-civilization/6414749001/ |archive-date=May 10, 2022 |access-date=June 7, 2022 |work=[[USA Today]] |ref=none}}|4={{Cite news |last1=Christensen |first1=Jen |date=August 30, 2022 |title=Elon Musk thinks the population will collapse. Demographers say it's not happening |url=https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/30/health/elon-musk-population-collapse-wellness/index.html |access-date=October 13, 2024 |publisher=[[CNN]] |ref=none}}}}</ref> and believes in the principles of [[Christianity]].<ref name="O'Mahony2024">{{cite web |last1=O'Mahony |first1=Catherine |date=July 26, 2024 |title=Elon Musk says he's a 'cultural Christian' – why some leading thinkers are embracing Christianity |url=https://www.tcd.ie/news_events/articles/2024/elon-musk-says-hes-a-cultural-christian--why-some-leading-thinkers-are-embracing-christianity |access-date=February 4, 2025 |publisher=[[Trinity College Dublin]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Walker |first1=Andrew T. |date=July 24, 2024 |title=Yet another champion for "cultural Christianity" |url=https://wng.org/opinions/yet-another-champion-for-cultural-christianity-1721817015 |access-date=February 4, 2025 |work=[[World (magazine)|World Magazine]] |language=en}}</ref> Musk has long been an advocate for [[space colonization]], especially the [[colonization of Mars]]. He has repeatedly pushed for humanity colonizing Mars, in order to become an interplanetary species and lower the risks of [[human extinction]].<ref name="SpaceX">{{cite web |title=Mars & Beyond: The Road to Making Humanity Interplanetary |url=https://www.spacex.com/human-spaceflight/mars/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221224072526/https://www.spacex.com/human-spaceflight/mars/ |archive-date=December 24, 2022 |access-date=December 27, 2022 |publisher=[[SpaceX]]}}</ref>

Musk has [[Views of Elon Musk#Conspiracy theories|promoted conspiracy theories]] and [[Views of Elon Musk#Race and white nationalism|made controversial statements]] that have led to accusations of [[racism]], [[sexism]], [[antisemitism]],<ref>{{Cite news |last=Rosenberg |first=Yair |date=May 16, 2023 |title=Elon Musk Among the Anti-Semites |url=https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2023/05/elon-musk-george-soros-anti-semites/674072/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230604030035/https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2023/05/elon-musk-george-soros-anti-semites/674072/ |archive-date=June 4, 2023 |access-date=June 5, 2023 |website=The Atlantic |language=en}}</ref><ref name="Truth">{{multiref2 |1={{cite web |url=https://www.mediaite.com/tech/elon-musk-agrees-with-poster-who-says-jews-advocate-hatred-against-whites/ |title=Elon Musk Agrees With Poster Who Says Jews Advocate 'Hatred Against Whites' |last=Bowers Bahney |first=Jennifer |date=November 15, 2023 |website=[[Mediaite]] |access-date=November 15, 2023 |archive-date=November 15, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231115231425/https://www.mediaite.com/tech/elon-musk-agrees-with-poster-who-says-jews-advocate-hatred-against-whites/ |url-status=live |ref=none}} |2={{Cite tweet |user=elonmusk |number=1724908287471272299 |title=You have said the actual truth |access-date=November 15, 2023 |ref=none}} |3={{cite magazine |url=https://time.com/6336123/elon-musk-antisemitic-post-x/ |title=Elon Musk Replies to Antisemitic Post on X, Labeling It 'The Actual Truth' |date=November 16, 2023 |magazine=Time |access-date=November 16, 2023 |archive-date=November 16, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231116135128/https://time.com/6336123/elon-musk-antisemitic-post-x/ |url-status=live}} |4={{Cite news |url=https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2023/11/elon-musks-disturbing-truth/676019/ |title=Elon Musk's Disturbing 'Truth' |date=November 16, 2023 |work=The Atlantic |acce