ld/americas/anti-vaccine-canada-truckers-roll-toward-ottawa-praised-by-teslas-musk-2022-01-27/ |archive-date=January 27, 2022 |access-date=April 27, 2022 |publisher=[[Reuters]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Ling |first1=Justin |date=February 8, 2022 |title=5G and QAnon: how conspiracy theorists steered Canada's anti-vaccine trucker protest |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/feb/08/canada-ottawa-trucker-protest-extremist-qanon-neo-nazi |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220208080607/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/feb/08/canada-ottawa-trucker-protest-extremist-qanon-neo-nazi |archive-date=February 8, 2022 |work=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref> He has amplified false claims of [[white genocide]] in South Africa.<ref>{{Cite news|last1=Hutzler|first1=Alexandra|last2=Walsh|first2=Kelsey|date=May 21, 2025|title=Trump confronts South Africa's president in Oval Office, pushes false claims of white genocide|work=ABC News|url=https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/trump-host-south-africas-president-amid-tensions-us/story?id=122002870|access-date=May 21, 2025|quote=Elon Musk, a South African native and a top adviser to the president during his second term who has also amplified false claims of "white genocide," was present for Ramaphosa's visit to the White House.}}</ref>

