Musk has been critical of Israel's [[Israeli invasion of the Gaza Strip|actions]] in the [[Gaza Strip]] during the [[Gaza war]],<ref name="Robertson-20232">{{Cite news |last=Robertson |first=Nick |date=November 10, 2023 |title=Elon Musk says Israel could thwart Hamas with 'conspicuous acts of kindness' |url=https://thehill.com/policy/international/4304954-elon-musk-israel-thwart-hamas-with-acts-of-kindness/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250113190958/https://thehill.com/policy/international/4304954-elon-musk-israel-thwart-hamas-with-acts-of-kindness/ |archive-date=January 13, 2025 |access-date=February 8, 2025 |work=[[The Hill (magazine)|The Hill]] |language=en-US}}</ref> praised China's economic and climate goals,<ref name="He-20212">{{cite news |last=He |first=Laura |date=March 24, 2021 |title=Elon Musk is trying to win China back |url=https://www.cnn.com/2021/03/24/tech/elon-musk-china-intl-hnk/index.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210709182137/https://www.cnn.com/2021/03/24/tech/elon-musk-china-intl-hnk/index.html |archive-date=July 9, 2021 |access-date=July 1, 2021 |publisher=[[CNN]]}}</ref><ref name="Choi-20192">{{Cite news |last=Choi |first=Martin |date=January 10, 2019 |title=Tesla boss Elon Musk says he loves China, so Premier Li Keqiang offers him a green card |url=https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/2181556/tesla-boss-elon-musk-says-he-loves-china-so-premier-li-keqiang |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190110124357/https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/2181556/tesla-boss-elon-musk-says-he-loves-china-so-premier-li-keqiang |archive-date=January 10, 2019 |access-date=December 20, 2024 |work=[[South China Morning Post]]}}</ref> suggested that [[Taiwan]] and China should resolve [[cross-strait relations]],<ref name="Liang-20222">{{cite news |last1=Liang |first1=Annabelle |date=October 10, 2022 |title=Elon Musk wades into China and Taiwan tensions |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/business-63196452 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221010034740/https://www.bbc.com/news/business-63196452 |archive-date=October 10, 2022 |access-date=October 10, 2022 |publisher=[[BBC News]]}}</ref><ref name="Khalaf-20222">{{cite news |last1=Khalaf |first1=Roula |date=October 7, 2022 |title=Elon Musk: 'Aren't you entertained?' |url=https://www.ft.com/content/5ef14997-982e-4f03-8548-b5d67202623a |archive-url=https://archive.today/20240514060142/https://www.ft.com/content/5ef14997-982e-4f03-8548-b5d67202623a |archive-date=May 14, 2024 |access-date=December 21, 2024 |work=[[Financial Times]]}}</ref> and was described as having a close relationship with the [[Chinese government]].<ref name="He-20212" /><ref name="Choi-20192" />

In Europe, Musk expressed support for Ukraine in 2022 during the [[Russian invasion of Ukraine|Russian invasion]], recommended referendums and peace deals on the annexed [[Russian-occupied territories of Ukraine|Russia-occupied territories]],<ref name="Oshin-20222">{{Cite web |last=Oshin |first=Olafimihan |date=March 14, 2022 |title=Elon Musk challenges Putin on Twitter to 'single combat' for Ukraine |url=https://thehill.com/policy/international/europe/598125-elon-musk-challenges-putin-on-twitter-to-single-combat-for/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221015172412/https://thehill.com/policy/international/europe/598125-elon-musk-challenges-putin-on-twitter-to-single-combat-for/ |archive-date=October 15, 2022 |access-date=October 29, 2024 |website=[[The Hill (newspaper)|The Hill]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name="Wilson-20222">{{Cite news |last=Wilson |first=Joseph |date=October 4, 2022 |title=Musk's plan to end Russian war infuriates Ukraine on Twitter |url=https://abcnews.go.com/Business/wireStory/musks-plan-end-russian-war-infuriates-ukraine-twitter-91000281 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221020101000/https://abcnews.go.com/Business/wireStory/musks-plan-end-russian-war-infuriates-ukraine-twitter-91000281 |archive-date=October 20, 2022 |access-date=October 16, 2022 |work=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]] |language=en |agency=Associated Press}}</ref> and supported the far-right [[Alternative for Germany]] in Germany in 2024.<ref name="Gold-20242">{{cite web |last=Gold |first=Hadas |date=December 20, 2024 |title=Elon Musk endorses far-right German political party, wading deeper into global politics |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2024/12/20/media/elon-musk-afd-germany-politics-far-right/index.html |access-date=December 23, 2024 |publisher=[[CNN]]}}</ref> Regarding [[British politics]], Musk blamed the [[2024 United Kingdom riots|2024 UK riots]] on [[mass migration]] and [[open border]]s,<ref name="Gregory-20242">{{cite news |last1=Gregory |first1=Andy |last2=Cooke |first2=Millie |date=August 5, 2024 |title=Downing Street condemns Elon Musk for claim 'civil war is inevitable' |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/home-news/elon-musk-civil-war-uk-riots-b2591213.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240805174350/https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/home-news/elon-musk-civil-war-uk-riots-b2591213.html |archive-date=August 5, 2024 |access-date=November 19, 2024 |newspaper=[[The Independent]]}}</ref><ref name="BBC News-2024a2">{{cite web |date=August 7, 2024 |title=What is Elon Musk's game plan? |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cze5gd1jzkeo |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240807125803/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cze5gd1jzkeo |archive-date=August 7, 2024 |access-date=November 19, 2024 |publisher=[[BBC News]]}}</ref> criticized Prime Minister [[Keir Starmer]] for what he described as a "two-tier" policing system,<ref name="The Independent-20242">{{Cite web |date=August 8, 2024 |title=Elon Musk lashes out at the UK again as Sunak holidays in California |first=David |last=Maddox|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/politics/elon-musk-riots-rishi-sunak-b2593155.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240809041242/https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/politics/elon-musk-riots-rishi-sunak-b2593155.html |archive-date=August 9, 2024 |access-date=January 14, 2025 |website=[[The Independent]]}}</ref><ref name="The Daily Telegraph-20242">{{cite news |date=August 6, 2024|first1=Martin|last1=Evans|first2=Cameron|last2=Henderson|first3=Dominic|last3=Penna|title=Musk brands Starmer 'two-tier Keir' amid row over riot policing |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2024/08/06/riots-police-tackle-all-sides-equal-ferocity-two-tier/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240807004921/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2024/08/06/riots-police-tackle-all-sides-equal-ferocity-two-tier/ |archive-date=August 7, 2024 |access-date=August 7, 2024 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]]}}</ref><ref name="BBC News-2024a2" /> and was subsequently attacked as being responsible for spreading [[misinformation]] and amplifying the far-right.<ref name="BBC News2">{{cite news |last1=Francis |first1=Sam |last2=Zeffman |first2=Henry |date=January 6, 2025 |title=PM attacks those 'spreading lies' on grooming gangs as he hits back at Musk |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c75wp53vk1lo |publisher=[[BBC News]]}}</ref> He has also voiced his support for far-right activist [[Tommy Robinson]] and pledged electoral support for [[Reform UK]].<ref name="BBC News-20252">{{Cite web |date=January 5, 2025 |title=Elon Musk calls for Nigel Farage to be replaced as Reform UK leader |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c70ep8lp4jjo |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250105144056/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c70ep8lp4jjo |archive-date=January 5, 2025 |access-date=January 5, 2025 |publisher=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref name="Turvill-20242">{{Cite web |last1=Turvill |first1=William |last2=Shipman |first2=Tim |last3=Wheeler |first3=Caroline |date=November 30, 2024 |title=Will Elon Musk give Nigel Farage $100m to make him PM? |url=https://www.thetimes.com/uk/politics/article/elon-musk-pay-nigel-farage-prime-minister-xts720xsp?t=1733042174755 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250127031718/https://www.thetimes.com/uk/politics/article/elon-musk-pay-nigel-farage-prime-minister-xts720xsp?t=1733042174755 |archive-date=January 27, 2025 |access-date=February 6, 2025 |website=[[The Times]] |language=en}}</ref>

