In 2018, Musk was [[Tesla, Inc.#Lawsuits and controversies|sued]] by the [[U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission]] (SEC) for a [[Tweet (social media)|tweet]] stating that funding had been secured for potentially taking Tesla private.<ref name="Goldstein_27-9-18">{{cite news |last=Goldstein |first=Matthew |date=September 27, 2018 |title=Tesla Chief Elon Musk Is Sued by S.E.C. in Move That Could Oust Him |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/27/business/elon-musk-sec-lawsuit-tesla.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200623023744/https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/27/business/elon-musk-sec-lawsuit-tesla.html |archive-date=June 23, 2020 |access-date=September 27, 2018 |work=The New York Times}}</ref>{{efn|Musk stated he was considering taking Tesla private at a price of $420 a share, an alleged reference to [[Cannabis (drug)|marijuana]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Choudhury |first=Saheli Roy |date=September 28, 2018 |title=SEC says Musk chose $420 price for Tesla shares because it's a pot reference |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2018/09/28/sec-says-elon-musk-at-tesla-chose-420-price-as-pot-reference.html |access-date=September 17, 2020 |publisher=CNBC |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201006010407/https://www.cnbc.com/2018/09/28/sec-says-elon-musk-at-tesla-chose-420-price-as-pot-reference.html |archive-date=October 6, 2020}}</ref> Members of Tesla's board and rapper [[Azealia Banks]] alleged that Musk may have been under the influence of recreational drugs when he wrote the tweet.<ref>{{cite news |last=Swisher |first=Kara |date=August 23, 2018 |title=How and Why Silicon Valley Gets High |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2018/08/23/opinion/elon-musk-burning-man-drugs-lsd.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180824014428/https://www.nytimes.com/2018/08/23/opinion/elon-musk-burning-man-drugs-lsd.html |archive-date=August 24, 2018 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |work=The New York Times |access-date=May 11, 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Woodyard |first=Chris |date=August 30, 2018 |title=Elon Musk's tweet on taking Tesla private now dogged by drugs claim from rapper Azealia Banks |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/talkingtech/2018/08/22/elon-musks-tweet-taking-tesla-private-now-dogged-drugs-claims-rapper-azealia-banks/1057815002/ |work=USA Today |access-date=May 11, 2021 |archive-date=May 12, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210512060023/https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/talkingtech/2018/08/22/elon-musks-tweet-taking-tesla-private-now-dogged-drugs-claims-rapper-azealia-banks/1057815002/ |url-status=live}}</ref>}} The securities fraud lawsuit characterized the tweet as false, misleading, and damaging to investors, and sought to bar Musk from serving as CEO of [[Public company|publicly traded companies]].<ref name="Goldstein_27-9-18" /><ref>{{cite news |last1=Patnaik |first1=Subrat |last2=Kalia |first2=Shubham |date=September 28, 2018 |title=Factbox – 'Funding secured': SEC gives timeline surrounding tweet from Tesla's Musk |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-tesla-musk-factbox/factbox-funding-secured-sec-gives-timeline-surrounding-tweet-from-teslas-musk-idUSKCN1M8139 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191123175743/https://www.reuters.com/article/us-tesla-musk-factbox/factbox-funding-secured-sec-gives-timeline-surrounding-tweet-from-teslas-musk-idUSKCN1M8139 |archive-date=November 23, 2019 |access-date=November 23, 2018 |publisher=Reuters}}</ref><ref name="OkaneLopatto18">{{cite news |last1=O'Kane |first1=Sean |last2=Lopatto |first2=Elizabeth |date=September 27, 2018 |title=Elon Musk sued by SEC for securities fraud |url=https://www.theverge.com/2018/9/27/17911428/sec-lawsuit-elon-musk-tesla-funding-tweet |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200730025451/https://www.theverge.com/2018/9/27/17911428/sec-lawsuit-elon-musk-tesla-funding-tweet |archive-date=July 30, 2020 |access-date=September 27, 2018 |work=The Verge}}</ref> Two days later, Musk settled with the SEC, without admitting or denying the SEC's allegations. As a result, Musk and Tesla were fined $20&nbsp;million each, and Musk was forced to step down for three years as Tesla chairman but was able to remain as CEO.<ref name=":7">{{Cite news |title=Elon Musk forced to step down as chairman of Tesla, remains CEO |url=https://www.theverge.com/2018/9/29/17918252/elon-musk-tesla-sec-securities-fraud-lawsuit-settlement-fine-penalty |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200527131445/https://www.theverge.com/2018/9/29/17918252/elon-musk-tesla-sec-securities-fraud-lawsuit-settlement-fine-penalty |archive-date=May 27, 2020 |access-date=September 29, 2018 |work=The Verge}}</ref> Shareholders filed a lawsuit over the tweet,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Brodkin |first=Jon |date=April 18, 2022 |title=Musk keeps falsely claiming 'Funding secured' tweet was accurate, judge is told |url=https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2022/04/judge-ruled-elon-musks-funding-secured-tweet-was-false-plaintiffs-say/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220909181731/https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2022/04/judge-ruled-elon-musks-funding-secured-tweet-was-false-plaintiffs-say/ |archive-date=September 9, 2022 |access-date=September 9, 2022 |website=Ars Technica |language=en-us}}</ref> and in February 2023, a jury found Musk and Tesla not liable.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Godoy |first1=Jody |last2=Jin |first2=Hyunjoo |date=February 3, 2023 |title=Tesla's Elon Musk found not liable in trial over 2018 'funding secured' tweets |url=https://www.reuters.com/legal/securities-fraud-trial-over-elon-musks-2018-tweets-draws-close-2023-02-03/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230204033538/https://www.reuters.com/legal/securities-fraud-trial-over-elon-musks-2018-tweets-draws-close-2023-02-03/ |archive-date=February 4, 2023 |access-date=February 4, 2023 |publisher=Reuters |language=en}}</ref> Musk has stated in interviews that he does not regret posting the tweet that triggered the SEC investigation.<ref>{{Cite news |date=October 27, 2018 |title=Tesla's Elon Musk says tweet that led to $20&nbsp;million fine 'Worth It' |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-tesla-musk-tweet-idUSKCN1N10K2 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200522093710/https://www.reuters.com/article/us-tesla-musk-tweet-idUSKCN1N10K2 |archive-date=May 22, 2020 |access-date=December 9, 2018 |publisher=Reuters}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Youn |first1=Soo |last2=Katersky |first2=Aaron |date=October 11, 2018 |title=Elon Musk commits to SEC settlement despite mocking tweets |url=https://abcnews.go.com/Business/elon-musk-commits-sec-settlement-mocking-tweets/story?id=58437587 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191023054443/https://abcnews.go.com/Business/elon-musk-commits-sec-settlement-mocking-tweets/story?id=58437587 |archive-date=October 23, 2019 |access-date=October 17, 2018 |publisher=ABC News}}</ref>

In 2019, Musk stated in a tweet that Tesla would build half&nbsp;a&nbsp;million cars that year.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Ohnsman |first=Alan |date=February 25, 2019 |title=Elon Musk's Tesla Tweet Puts CEO Role at Risk Again |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/alanohnsman/2019/02/25/elon-musks-tesla-tweet-puts-ceo-role-at-risk-again/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200528012956/https://www.forbes.com/sites/alanohnsman/2019/02/25/elon-musks-tesla-tweet-puts-ceo-role-at-risk-again/ |archive-date=May 28, 2020 |access-date=February 26, 2019 |work=Forbes}}</ref> The SEC reacted by asking a court to hold him [[Contempt of court|in contempt]] for violating the terms of the 2018 settlement agreement. A joint agreement between Musk and the SEC eventually clarified the previous agreement details,<ref>{{Cite news |last=Wattles |first=Jackie |date=April 27, 2019 |title=Elon Musk and SEC reach an agreement over tweeting |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2019/04/26/tech/elon-musk-sec-settlement/index.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200608013859/https://edition.cnn.com/2019/04/26/tech/elon-musk-sec-settlement/index.html |archive-date=June 8, 2020 |access-date=July 16, 2019 |publisher=CNN Business}}</ref> including a list of topics about which Musk needed preclearance.<ref>{{cite news |last=Marino-Nachison |first=David |date=April 26, 2019 |title=Tesla CEO Elon Musk Gets a Long Do-Not-Tweet List From the SEC |url=https://www.barrons.com/articles/tesla-ceo-elon-musk-sec-settlement-list-51556317578?mod=article_inline |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200122145614/https://www.barrons.com/articles/tesla-ceo-elon-musk-sec-settlement-list-51556317578?mod=article_inline |archive-date=January 22, 2020 |access-date=November 25, 2019 |work=Barron's}}</ref> In 2020, a judge blocked a lawsuit that claimed a tweet by Musk regarding Tesla stock price ("too high [[List of acronyms: I|imo]]") violated the agreement.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Bursztynsky |first=Jessica |date=May 1, 2020 |title=Tesla shares tank after Elon Musk tweets the stock price is 'too high' |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2020/05/01/tesla-ceo-elon-musk-says-stock-price-is-too-high-shares-fall.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200818102755/https://www.cnbc.com/2020/05/01/tesla-ceo-elon-musk-says-stock-price-is-too-high-shares-fall.html |archive-date=August 18, 2020 |access-date=June 14, 2020 |publisher=CNBC}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=May 20, 2020 |title=Court Rules That No One Can Stop Elon Musk From Tweeting Tesla News—For Now |url=https://observer.com/2020/05/tesla-shareholder-lawsuit-stop-elon-musk-tweeting-on-hold/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201030161912/https://observer.com/2020/05/tesla-shareholder-lawsuit-stop-elon-musk-tweeting-on-hold/ |archive-date=October 30, 2020 |access-date=December 1, 2020 |work=The Observer}}</ref> [[Freedom of Information Act (United States)|Freedom of Information Act]] (FOIA)-released records showed that the SEC concluded Musk had subsequently violated the agreement twice by tweeting regarding "[[Tesla Energy|Tesla's solar roof]] production volumes and its stock price".<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Elliott |first1=Dave |last2=Michaels |first2=Rebecca |date=June 2, 2021 |title=WSJ News Exclusive: Tesla Failed to Oversee Elon Musk's Tweets, SEC Argued in Letters |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/tesla-failed-to-oversee-elon-musk-s-tweets-sec-argued-in-letters-11622582765 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210610030929/https://www.wsj.com/articles/tesla-failed-to-oversee-elon-musk-s-tweets-sec-argued-in-letters-11622582765 |archive-date=June 10, 2021 |access-date=June 10, 2021 |work=The Wall Street Journal}}</ref>

In October 2023, the SEC sued Musk over his refusal to testify a third time in an investigation into whether he violated federal law by purchasing Twitter stock in 2022.<ref name="Brodkin-2023">{{Cite web |last=Brodkin |first=Jon |date=October 6, 2023 |title=Musk refused to testify in Twitter stock probe, claimed SEC is harassing him |url=https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2023/10/sec-sues-musk-saying-he-refuses-to-testify-in-twitter-stock-investigation/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231013040318/https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2023/10/sec-sues-musk-saying-he-refuses-to-testify-in-twitter-stock-investigation/ |archive-date=October 13, 2023 |access-date=October 7, 2023 |website=Ars Technica |language=en-us}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Fung |first1=Brian |last2=Duffy |first2=Clare |date=October 5, 2023 |title=US regulator seeks court order to compel Elon Musk to testify about his Twitter acquisition |url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/10/05/tech/elon-musk-sec-twitter-lawsuit/index.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231018114814/https://www.cnn.com/2023/10/05/tech/elon-musk-sec-twitter-lawsuit/index.html |archive-date=October 18, 2023 |access-date=October 7, 2023 |publisher=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref><ref name="Regulator sues Musk to force testimony in X probe-2023">{{Cite news |date=October 5, 2023 |title=Regulator sues Musk to force testimony in X probe |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/business-67024538 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022231748/https://www.bbc.com/news/business-67024538 |archive-date=October 22, 2023 |access-date=October 7, 2023 |publisher=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> In February 2024, Judge Laurel Beeler ruled that Musk must testify again.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Godoy |first=Jody |date=February 12, 2024 |title=US judge orders Elon Musk to testify in SEC's Twitter probe |url=https://www.reuters.com/legal/elon-musk-ordered-testify-secs-twitter-probe-2024-02-11/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240219011742/https://www.reuters.com/legal/elon-musk-ordered-testify-secs-twitter-probe-2024-02-11/ |archive-date=February 19, 2024 |access-date=April 21, 2024 |publisher=Reuters}}</ref> In January 2025, the SEC filed a lawsuit against Musk for securities violations related to his purchase of Twitter.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Goldstein |first1=Matthew |last2=Conger |first2=Kate |date=January 14, 2025 |title=S.E.C. Sues Elon Musk Over Twitter-Related Securities Violations |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/14/technology/sec-elon-musk-securities-violations.html |website=The New York Times}}</ref> In January 2024, Delaware judge [[Kathaleen McCormick]] ruled in a 2018 lawsuit that Musk's $55&nbsp;billion pay package from Tesla be rescinded.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Mangan |first1=Dan |author2=Lora Kolodny |author-link2=Lora Kolodny |date=January 30, 2024 |title=Elon Musk's $56 billion Tesla compensation voided by judge, shares slide |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2024/01/30/tesla-shares-slide-after-judge-voids-elon-musks-56-billion-compensation.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240131002140/https://www.cnbc.com/2024/01/30/tesla-shares-slide-after-judge-voids-elon-musks-56-billion-compensation.html |archive-date=January 31, 2024 |access-date=January 31, 2024 |publisher=CNBC |language=en}}</ref> McCormick called the compensation granted by the company's board "an unfathomable sum" that was unfair to shareholders.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Kharpal |first1=Arjun |author2=Lora Kolodny |author-link2=Lora Kolodny |date=February 1, 2024 |title=Elon Musk says Tesla will hold a shareholder vote to incorporate in Texas after Delaware pay snub |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2024/02/01/elon-musk-tesla-will-hold-a-shareholder-vote-to-incorporate-in-texas.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240206032239/https://www.cnbc.com/2024/02/01/elon-musk-tesla-will-hold-a-shareholder-vote-to-incorporate-in-texas.html |archive-date=February 6, 2024 |access-date=February 6, 2024 |publisher=CNBC |language=en}}</ref>

==Personal life==
Musk became a U.S. citizen in 2002.<ref name=":6">{{cite news |last1=Shoichet |first1=Catherine E. |title=Elon Musk is one of illegal immigration's harshest critics. He once described his past immigration status as a 'gray area' |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2024/09/29/us/elon-musk-immigration-gray-area-cec/index.html |publisher=[[CNN]] |date=September 29, 2024 |access-date=November 19, 2024 |archive-date=November 13, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241113024641/https://edition.cnn.com/2024/09/29/us/elon-musk-immigration-gray-area-cec/index.html |url-status=live}}</ref> From the early 2000s until late 2020, Musk resided in California, where both Tesla and SpaceX were founded.<ref name="bloomberg20201208">{{cite news |date=December 8, 2020 |title=Musk Relocates to Texas, Criticizes 'Complacent' California |publisher=Bloomberg L.P. |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2020-12-08/tesla-ceo-elon-musk-says-he-has-relocated-to-texas |url-status=live |access-date=December 9, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201210145135/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2020-12-08/tesla-ceo-elon-musk-says-he-has-relocated-to-texas |archive-date=December 10, 2020}}</ref> He then relocated to [[Cameron County, Texas]],<ref>{{cite tweet |last=Musk |first=Elon |user=elonmusk |number=1402718368633745410 |date=June 9, 2021 |title=My primary home is literally a ~$50k house in Boca Chica / Starbase that I rent from SpaceX. It's kinda awesome though.}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Williams |first=Claudia |date=June 25, 2024 |title=Where Does Elon Musk Live? Inside the Properties of the World's Richest Man |website=Architectural Digest |url=https://www.architecturaldigest.com/story/where-does-elon-musk-live}}</ref> saying that California had become "complacent" about its economic success.<ref name="bloomberg20201208" /><ref>{{cite news |last=Somerville |first=Heather |date=December 8, 2020 |title=Elon Musk Moves to Texas, Takes Jab at Silicon Valley |work=The Wall Street Journal |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/elon-musk-to-discuss-teslas-banner-year-despite-pandemic-silicon-valleys-future-11607449988 |url-status=live |access-date=December 13, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201212234036/https://www.wsj.com/articles/elon-musk-to-discuss-teslas-banner-year-despite-pandemic-silicon-valleys-future-11607449988 |archive-date=December 12, 2020}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Milmo |first=Dan |date=August 31, 2023 |title=Tesla investigated over funds 'used to build secret Austin house for Elon Musk' |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/aug/31/tesla-investigated-over-funds-used-to-build-secret-austin-house-for-elon-musk |access-date=April 30, 2024 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

While hosting ''[[Saturday Night Live]]'' in 2021, Musk stated that he has [[Asperger syndrome]] (now merged with [[Autism|autism spectrum disorder]]).<ref>{{Cite news |last=Yahr |first=Emily |date=May 8, 2021 |title=Elon Musk reveals he has Asperger's syndrome during SNL monologue |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/arts-entertainment/2021/05/09/elon-musk-hosts-snl/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210509204204/https://www.washingtonpost.com/arts-entertainment/2021/05/09/elon-musk-hosts-snl/ |archive-date=May 9, 2021 |access-date=May 9, 2021 |newspaper=The Washington Post}}</ref><ref>[[#Isaacson|Isaacson (2023)]], p. 18.</ref> When asked about his experience growing up with Asperger's syndrome in a TED2022 conference in Vancouver, Musk stated that "the social cues were not intuitive ... I would just tend to take things very literally ... but then that turned out to be wrong — [people were not] simply saying exactly what they mean, there's all sorts of other things that are meant, and [it] took me a while to figure that out."<ref>{{cite web |last1=King |first1=Hope |title=Elon Musk opens up about growing up with Asperger's |url=https://www.axios.com/2022/04/15/elon-musk-aspergers-syndrome |website=Axios |language=en |date=April 15, 2022}}</ref> Musk suffers from back pain and has undergone several spine-related surgeries, including a [[Intervertebral disc|disc]] replacement.<ref>{{Cite news |last=IANS |date=April 16, 2024 |title=Elon Musk shares health advice on severe neck and back pain |url=https://www.thestatesman.com/technology/elon-musk-shares-health-advice-on-severe-neck-and-back-pain-1503290796.html |access-date=January 19, 2025 |website=The Statesman |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=August 7, 2023 |title=Musk Says He May Need Surgery, Will Get MRI on Back and Neck |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-08-07/musk-says-he-may-need-surgery-will-get-mri-on-back-and-neck |access-date=January 19, 2025 |work=Bloomberg.com |language=en}}</ref> In 2000, he contracted a severe case of [[malaria]] while on vacation in South Africa.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Locke |first=Taylor |date=November 2, 2019 |title=Why Elon Musk says taking 'vacations will kill you' |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2019/11/02/why-elon-musk-says-taking-vacations-will-kill-you.html |access-date=January 19, 2025 |publisher=CNBC |language=en}}</ref>

Musk has stated he uses doctor-prescribed [[ketamine]] for occasional depression and that he doses "a small amount once every other week or something like that";<ref>{{Cite news |last=Duffy |first=Clare |date=March 18, 2024 |title=Elon Musk details his prescription ketamine use, says investors should want him to 'keep taking it' {{!}} CNN Business |url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/03/18/tech/elon-musk-ketamine-use-don-lemon-interview/index.html |access-date=October 28, 2024 |publisher=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref> since January 2024, some media outlets have reported that he takes [[ketamine]], [[marijuana]], [[LSD]], [[ecstasy (drug)|ecstasy]], [[hallucinogenic mushrooms|mushrooms]], [[cocaine]] and other drugs. Musk at first refused to comment on his alleged drug use, before responding that he had not [[drug test|tested]] positive for drugs, and that if drugs somehow improved his productivity, "I would definitely take them!".<ref>Multiple sources:
