* [https://www.wsj.com/tech/elon-musk-criticizes-wsj-reporting-on-his-use-of-illegal-drugs-c268d0fb Elon Musk Criticizes WSJ Reporting on His Use of Illegal Drugs] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250212040049/https://www.wsj.com/tech/elon-musk-criticizes-wsj-reporting-on-his-use-of-illegal-drugs-c268d0fb}}, [[The Wall Street Journal]].
* [https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/elon-musk-used-illegal-drugs-sparked-concerns-among-tesla-spacex-board-members-report-4815677 Elon Musk Used LSD, Cocaine; Gave Slurred Speech At SpaceX Event: Report] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241201173748/https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/elon-musk-used-illegal-drugs-sparked-concerns-among-tesla-spacex-board-members-report-4815677}}, [[NDTV]].
* [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NH4_rcq4jgQ Elon Musk uses LSD, cocaine, ecstasy, mushrooms: WSJ] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240516011424/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NH4_rcq4jgQ}}, [[Bloomberg Television]].</ref> ''[[The New York Times|The New York Times']]'' investigations revealed Musk's overuse of ketamine and numerous other drugs, as well as strained family relationships and concerns from close associates who have become troubled by his public behavior as he became more involved in political activities and government work.<ref>{{cite web|first1=Kirsten|last1=Grind|first2=Megan|last2=Twohey|date=May 30, 2025|title=On the Campaign Trail, Elon Musk Juggled Drugs and Family Drama|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/30/us/elon-musk-drugs-children-trump.html|work=The New York Times|access-date=May 31, 2025}}</ref> According to ''The Washington Post'', President Trump described Musk as "a big-time drug addict".<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Zakrzewski |first1=Cat |last2=Allison |first2=Natalie |last3=Dwoskin |first3=Elizabeth |last4=Stein |first4=Jeff |last5=Davies |first5=Emily |last6=Svitek |first6=Patrick |last7=Alfaro |first7=Mariana |last8=Tucker |first8=Brianna |last9=Cunningham |first9=Paige Winfield |date=June 7, 2025 |title=Inside the battles that shattered Trump and Musk's alliance |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2025/06/07/trump-elon-musk-fight-behind-scenes/ |access-date=June 17, 2025 |newspaper=The Washington Post |language=en-US |issn=0190-8286}}</ref>

Through his own label Emo G Records, Musk released a [[rap]] track, "RIP [[Harambe]]", on [[SoundCloud]] in March 2019.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Arcand |first1=Rob |date=March 31, 2019 |title=Elon Musk Drops Surprise Rap Single 'RIP Harambe' |url=https://www.spin.com/2019/03/elon-musk-drops-rap-single-rip-harambe/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190401021823/https://www.spin.com/2019/03/elon-musk-drops-rap-single-rip-harambe/ |archive-date=April 1, 2019 |access-date=April 1, 2019 |work=Spin}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Kreps |first=Daniel |date=March 31, 2019 |title=Hear Elon Musk's Surprise Rap Song 'RIP Harambe' |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/elon-musk-rap-song-rip-harambe-815813/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190403213417/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/elon-musk-rap-song-rip-harambe-815813/ |archive-date=April 3, 2019 |access-date=July 9, 2024 |magazine=Rolling Stone |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name="Fitzgerald">{{cite news |last1=Fitzgerald |first1=Trent |date=March 31, 2019 |title=Elon Musk Randomly Shares Rap Song Dedicated to Harambe |url=https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/03/elon-musk-rap-song-harambe/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190403145015/https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/03/elon-musk-rap-song-harambe/ |archive-date=April 3, 2019 |access-date=April 10, 2019 |work=XXL}}</ref> The following year, he released an [[Electronic dance music|EDM]] track, "Don't Doubt Ur Vibe", featuring his own lyrics and vocals.<ref name="Etherington">{{Cite news |last=Etherington |first=Darrell |title=Elon Musk just dropped an EDM track on SoundCloud |url=https://techcrunch.com/2020/01/31/elon-musk-just-dropped-an-edm-track-on-soundcloud/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210426204232/https://techcrunch.com/2020/01/31/elon-musk-just-dropped-an-edm-track-on-soundcloud/ |archive-date=April 26, 2021 |date=January 31, 2020 |work=[[TechCrunch]] }}</ref>

Musk plays video games, which he stated has a "'restoring effect' that helps his 'mental calibration'".<ref>{{cite news |last=Harwell |first=Drew |title=Elon Musk rose to the top of video game charts. Now he has confessed to cheating. |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2025/01/29/elon-musk-video-games-diablo-path-exile/ |newspaper=The Washington Post |access-date=February 4, 2025 |language=en |date=January 29, 2025}}</ref> Some games he plays include [[Quake (series)|''Quake'']], ''[[Diablo IV]]'', ''[[Elden Ring]]'', and [[The Battle of Polytopia|''Polytopia'']].<ref>{{Cite news |date=October 23, 2023 |title=Elon Musk's Intense Obsession With A Video Game Influenced His Business Strategies, Caused Fights In His Relationship And Served As A Reminder Every Move Matters |url=https://finance.yahoo.com/news/elon-musks-intense-obsession-video-171328115.html#:~:text=His%20latest%20biography%20explains%20his,the%20game's%20developer%20Felix%20Ekenstam. |website=Yahoo Finance |access-date=April 21, 2024 |archive-date=November 11, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231111201452/https://finance.yahoo.com/news/elon-musks-intense-obsession-video-171328115.html#:~:text=His%20latest%20biography%20explains%20his,the%20game's%20developer%20Felix%20Ekenstam. |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=August 11, 2018 |title=Elon Musk loves video games. Here are 10 of his favorites |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-favorite-video-games-2017-6 |website=[[Business Insider]] |access-date=April 21, 2024 |archive-date=February 18, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240218165802/https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-favorite-video-games-2017-6 |url-status=live}}</ref> Musk once claimed to be one of the world's top video game players but has since admitted to "[[Boosting (video games)|account boosting]]", or cheating by hiring outside services to achieve top player rankings.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Holmes |first1=Oliver |title=Elon Musk admits cheating at video games, chat transcript appears to show |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jan/22/elon-musk-admits-cheating-at-video-games-chat-transcript-appears-to-show |website=[[The Guardian]] |date=January 22, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=January 30, 2025 |title=Gamers Disgusted as Elon Musk Admits to Cheating at Video Games After Bragging About Being Top Player |url=https://futurism.com/gamers-disgusted-musk-cheats-diablo-path-exile |access-date=February 2, 2025 |website=Futurism}}</ref><ref name= "Gizmodo Paying" >{{cite web |last=Gault |first=Matthew |title=Elon Musk Admits to Paying People to Play Video Games for Him |url=https://gizmodo.com/elon-musk-admits-to-paying-people-to-play-video-games-for-him-2000552872 |website=gizmodo.com |date=January 21, 2025 |publisher=Gizmodo |access-date=March 26, 2025}}</ref> Musk has justified the boosting by claiming that all top accounts do it so he has to as well to remain competitive.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Gach |first1=Ethan |title=Elon Musk Admits To Cheating In Path Of Exile 2 And Diablo 4 Amid Fake Gamer Controversy |url=https://kotaku.com/elon-musk-poe2-diablo-4-paid-boosting-fake-controversy-1851743670 |website=kotaku.com |date=January 21, 2025 |publisher=Kotaku |access-date=March 26, 2025}}</ref><ref name= "Gizmodo Paying" /><ref>{{cite web |last1=Tan |first1=Eli |last2=Isaac |first2=Mike |title=Elon Musk, video game king? Well, maybe not |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/26/technology/elon-musk-video-games-diablo-path-of-exile.html |website=[[The New York Times]] |date=January 26, 2025 |access-date=March 26, 2025}}</ref> In 2024 and 2025, Musk criticized the video game ''[[Assassin's Creed Shadows]]'' and its creator [[Ubisoft]] for "woke" content.<ref name= "PC Gamer Ratio" >{{cite web |last1=Randall |first1=Harvey |title=Ubisoft scores a legendary ratio against Elon Musk on his own platform—which hopefully marks a final end to all the Assassin's Creed Shadows' culture war nonsense |url=https://www.pcgamer.com/games/assassins-creed/ubisoft-scores-a-legendary-ratio-against-elon-musk-on-his-own-platform-which-hopefully-marks-a-final-end-to-all-the-assassins-creed-shadows-culture-war-nonsense/ |website=pcgamer.com |date=March 26, 2025 |publisher=PC Gamer}}</ref> Musk posted to X that "DEI kills art" and specified the inclusion of the historical figure [[Yasuke]] in the ''Assassin's Creed'' game as offensive; he also called the game "terrible". Ubisoft responded by saying that Musk's comments were "just feeding hatred" and that they were focused on producing a game not pushing politics.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Bošnjak |first1=Dominik |title=Ubisoft Responds to Elon Musk's Assassin's Creed Shadows Criticism |url=https://gamerant.com/assassins-creed-shadows-elon-musk-woke-criticism-ubisoft-response/ |website=gamerant.com |date=June 13, 2024 |publisher=Game Rant |access-date=March 26, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Bošnjak |first1=Dominik |title=Assassin's Creed Throws Shade at Elon Musk After Hasan Comments |url=https://gamerant.com/assassins-creed-shadows-elon-musk-burn-path-of-exile-hasan-comments/ |website=gamerant.com |date=March 26, 2025 |publisher=Game Rant |access-date=March 26, 2025}}</ref>

===Relationships and children===
{{Further|Musk family}}
[[File:X Æ A-Xii, Elon Musk and Donald Trump in the Oval Office - P20250207DT-0103 (54320797642).jpg|thumb|thumbtime=182|upright=1|Musk with his son, X Æ A-Xii, in the [[Oval Office]], February 11, 2025]]
Musk has fathered at least 14 children, one of whom died as an infant.<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Wickman |first1=Kase |title=Elon Musk's 14 Children and Their Mothers (That We Know Of): A Handy Guide |url=https://www.vanityfair.com/style/story/all-elon-musk-children-and-mothers |magazine=Vanity Fair |date=March 5, 2025 }}</ref> ''The Wall Street Journal'' reported in 2025 that sources close to Musk suggest that the "true number of Musk's children is much higher than publicly known".<ref name="Mattioli 16APR2025">{{cite web|url=https://www.wsj.com/politics/elon-musk-children-mothers-ashley-st-clair-grimes-dc7ba05c|title=The Tactics Elon Musk Uses to Manage His 'Legion' of Babies—and Their Mothers|publisher=The Wall Street Journal|last=Mattioli|first=Dana|date=April 16, 2025|access-date=April 16, 2025|language=en}}</ref> He had six children with his first wife, Canadian author [[Justine Wilson]], who he met while attending Queen's University in Ontario, Canada; they married in 2000.<ref name="Streisand-2015">{{cite news |last=Durand Streisand |first=Elizabeth |title=A Look at Elon Musk's Rocky Romantic History |url=https://www.yahoo.com/celebrity/blogs/celeb-news/elon-musk-love-life-romantic-history-171340935.html |work=Yahoo |access-date=May 29, 2017 |archive-date=June 2, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200602025744/https://www.yahoo.com/entertainment/blogs/celeb-news/elon-musk-love-life-romantic-history-171340935.html}}</ref> In 2002, their first child Nevada Musk died of [[sudden infant death syndrome]] at the age of 10 weeks.<ref name="sids">[[#Vance|Vance (2017)]], p. 117.</ref> After his death, the couple used [[In vitro fertilisation|in vitro fertilization]] (IVF) to continue their family;<ref name="holywoodlife2021">{{cite news |last=Crowley |first=James |date=September 14, 2021 |title=Elon Musk's Kids: Meet His 6 Kids From Oldest To Youngest, & Their Moms |url=https://hollywoodlife.com/feature/elon-musk-kids-4516506/ |work=Hollywood Life |access-date=September 16, 2021 |archive-date=September 16, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210916014406/https://hollywoodlife.com/feature/elon-musk-kids-4516506/ |url-status=live}}</ref> they had twins in 2004, followed by triplets in 2006.<ref name="holywoodlife2021" /> The couple divorced in 2008 and have [[Joint custody (United States)|shared custody]] of their children.<ref>{{cite news |last=Musk |first=Justine |date=September 10, 2010 |title="I Was a Starter Wife": Inside America's Messiest Divorce |url=https://www.marieclaire.com/sex-love/a5380/millionaire-starter-wife/ |work=Marie Claire |access-date=September 3, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200730172806/https://www.marieclaire.com/sex-love/a5380/millionaire-starter-wife/ |archive-date=July 30, 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=April 27, 2015 |title=Elon Musk's Ex-Wife on What It Takes to Be a Mogul |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2015/04/28/business/dealbook/insider-offers-a-view-from-moguls-lofty-heights.html |work=The New York Times |access-date=June 26, 2022 |archive-date=June 26, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220626164639/https://www.nytimes.com/2015/04/28/business/dealbook/insider-offers-a-view-from-moguls-lofty-heights.html |url-status=live}}</ref> The elder twin he had with Wilson [[gender identity|came out]] as a [[trans woman]] and, in 2022, officially [[name change|changed her name]] to [[Vivian Wilson|Vivian Jenna Wilson]],<ref name="06-23-22">{{Cite news |date=June 23, 2022 |title=Elon Musk's daughter granted legal name, gender change |url=https://apnews.com/article/elon-musk-entertainment-gender-identity-santa-monica-eb64ed75c5e8228ca3cae8e1d836e93d |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220626091711/https://apnews.com/article/elon-musk-entertainment-gender-identity-santa-monica-eb64ed75c5e8228ca3cae8e1d836e93d |archive-date=June 26, 2022 |access-date=October 7, 2022 |publisher=Associated Press}}</ref> adopting her mother's surname because she no longer wished to be associated with Musk.<ref name="06-23-22" />

Musk began dating English actress [[Talulah Riley]] in 2008.<ref>[[#Vance|Vance (2017)]], pp. 193–195.</ref> They married two years later at [[Dornoch Cathedral]] in Scotland.<ref name="marriage">{{Cite news |agency=Associated Press |date=March 21, 2016 |title=Actor Talulah Riley files to divorce billionaire Elon Musk, again |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2016/mar/21/elon-musk-talulah-riley-file-divorce-second-marriage |newspaper=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=April 20, 2016 |archive-date=June 16, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180616231332/https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2016/mar/21/elon-musk-talulah-riley-file-divorce-second-marriage |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |first=Alan |last=Boyle |date=January 18, 2012 |title=SpaceX's millionaire founder tweets about marital split |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/science/spacexs-millionaire-founder-tweets-about-marital-split-6C10402497 |publisher=NBC News |access-date=September 28, 2013 |archive-date=July 1, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220701212028/https://www.nbcnews.com/science/spacexs-millionaire-founder-tweets-about-marital-split-6C10402497 |url-status=live}}</ref> In 2012, the couple divorced, then remarried the following year.<ref name="talulah" /> After briefly filing for divorce in 2014,<ref name="talulah">{{Cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2016/10/22/elon-musk-and-talulah-riley-divorce-for-a-second-time/ |title=Elon Musk and Talulah Riley divorce for a second time |date=October 22, 2016 |work=The Daily Telegraph |access-date=June 29, 2018 |archive-date=June 30, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180630004337/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2016/10/22/elon-musk-and-talulah-riley-divorce-for-a-second-time/ |url-status=live}}</ref> Musk finalized a second divorce from Riley in 2016.<ref>[[#Vance|Vance (2017)]], p. 372.</ref> Musk then dated the American actress [[Amber Heard]] for several months in 2017;<ref>{{cite news |last=Jensen |first=Erin |date=April 24, 2017 |title=Amber Heard, Elon Musk make 'Cheeky' public debut together |work=USA Today |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/entertainthis/2017/04/24/amber-heard-elon-musk-dating-public-debut-instagram-posts/100834568/ |access-date=January 28, 2021 |archive-date=January 30, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210130231024/https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/entertainthis/2017/04/24/amber-heard-elon-musk-dating-public-debut-instagram-posts/100834568/ |url-status=live}}</ref> he had reportedly been "pursuing" her since 2012.<ref name="hollywood">{{cite news |last=Sigel |first=Tatiana |date=December 6, 2018 |title=Amber Heard on Her Secret Passion, Elon Musk and a Splashy New Role |work=The Hollywood Reporter |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/features/amber-heard-aquaman-elon-musk-dedication-activism-1166004 |url-status=live |access-date=January 28, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181206185106/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/features/amber-heard-aquaman-elon-musk-dedication-activism-1166004 |archive-date=December 6, 2018}}</ref>

In 2018, Musk and Canadian musician [[Grimes]] confirmed they were dating.<ref>{{cite news |first=Jordan |last=Darville |title=Grimes talks new music, Elon Musk, plans to publicly execute her musical persona |url=https://www.thefader.com/2019/03/20/grimes-interview-miss-anthropocene |work=The Fader |date=March 20, 2019 |access-date=December 13, 2020 |archive-date=October 30, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191030070534/http://www.thefader.com/2019/03/20/grimes-interview-miss-anthropocene |url-status=live}}</ref> Grimes and Musk have three children, born in 2020, 2021, and 2022.<ref>{{cite news |last=Kiefer |first=Halle |title=Grimes and Elon Musk's Baby Has Arrived, Just As Legend Foretold |date=May 4, 2020 |url=https://www.vulture.com/2020/05/elon-musk-and-grimes-welcome-first-baby-together.html |work=Vulture |access-date=May 5, 2020 |url-access=limited |archive-date=May 5, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200505021026/https://www.vulture.com/2020/05/elon-musk-and-grimes-welcome-first-baby-together.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Trepany |first=Charles |title=Elon Musk shares first photo of his and Grimes' new baby boy: 'Mom and baby all good' |date=May 5, 2020 |url=https://eu.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2020/05/05/elon-musk-grimes-welcome-baby/3082615001/ |work=USA Today |access-date=May 5, 2020 |archive-date=May 29, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200529124947/https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2020/05/05/elon-musk-grimes-welcome-baby/3082615001/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/showbiz/elon-musk-third-child-grimes-name-techno-mechanicus-tau-b1106201.html |title=Elon Musk confirms third child with Grimes and shares newborn's unusual name |date=September 11, 2023 |last=Hines |first=Dominique |website=The Standard |access-date=February 13, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-grimes-child-techno-mechanicus-tau-2023-9 |title=New Elon Musk biography says he has 3rd child with Grimes named Techno Mechanicus |author1=Katie Hawkinson |author2=Grace Dean |date=September 11, 2023 |website=businessinsider.com}}</ref> Musk and Grimes originally gave their eldest child the name "X [[Æ]] A-12", which would have violated California regulations as it contained characters that are not in the modern English alphabet;<ref>{{cite news |last1=Schwedel |first1=Heather |title=What Does Elon Musk and Grimes' Baby Name Actually Mean? |url=https://slate.com/human-interest/2020/05/elon-musk-grimes-baby-name.html |access-date=May 5, 2020 |work=Slate |date=May 5, 2020 |archive-date=May 24, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200524150019/https://slate.com/human-interest/2020/05/elon-musk-grimes-baby-name.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Lerman |first=Rachel |date=May 8, 2020 |title=Elon Musk's baby name isn't just weird, it may be against California regulations |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2020/05/08/musk-grimes-baby-name/ |newspaper=The Washington Post |access-date=January 11, 2021 |archive-date=December 31, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201231225820/https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2020/05/08/musk-grimes-baby-name/ |url-status=live}}</ref> the names registered on the birth certificate are "X" as a first name, "Æ A-[[Roman numerals|Xii]]" as a middle name, and "Musk" as a last name.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Elon Musk and Grimes have changed their baby's name. A bit |first=Jack |last=Guy |url=https://www.cnn.com/2020/05/25/entertainment/grimes-musk-baby-name-tweak-scli-intl/index.html |publisher=[[CNN]] |date=May 25, 2020 |access-date=May 25, 2020 |archive-date=May 25, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200525204407/https://www.cnn.com/2020/05/25/entertainment/grimes-musk-baby-name-tweak-scli-intl/index.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="xaea-xii.cnet">{{cite news |last=Cooper |first=Gael Fashingbauer |date=June 16, 2020 |title=Elon Musk and Grimes saved a surprise for son X Æ A-12's birth certificate |url=https://www.cnet.com/news/elon-musk-and-grimes-saved-a-surprise-for-son-x-ae-a-12s-birth-certificate/ |publisher=CNET |access-date=June 17, 2020 |archive-date=June 17, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200617021513/https://www.cnet.com/news/elon-musk-and-grimes-saved-a-surprise-for-son-x-ae-a-12s-birth-certificate/ |url-status=live}}</ref> They received criticism for choosing a name perceived to be impractical and difficult to pronounce;<ref>{{Cite news |title=Elon Musk and Grimes' newborn name X Æ A-12 'fails at the basic job of being a name,' says author |url=https://www.cbc.ca/radio/thecurrent/the-current-for-may-7-2020-1.5559171/elon-musk-and-grimes-newborn-name-x-%C3%A6-a-12-fails-at-the-basic-job-of-being-a-name-says-author-1.5559761 |access-date=August 12, 2024 |publisher=CBC Radio |archive-date=August 12, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240812165748/https://www.cbc.ca/radio/thecurrent/the-current-for-may-7-2020-1.5559171/elon-musk-and-grimes-newborn-name-x-%C3%A6-a-12-fails-at-the-basic-job-of-being-a-name-says-author-1.5559761 |url-status=live}}</ref> Musk has said the intended pronunciation is "X Ash A Twelve".<ref name="xaea-xii.cnet" /> Their second child was born via [[surrogacy]].<ref name="GrimesVanityFair2022">{{cite magazine |last=Gordon |first=Devin |date=March 10, 2022 |title="Infamy Is Kind Of Fun": Grimes on Music, Mars, and—Surprise!—Her Secret New Baby With Elon Musk |url=https://www.vanityfair.com/style/2022/03/grimes-cover-story-on-music-and-mars |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220521235459/https://www.vanityfair.com/style/2022/03/grimes-cover-story-on-music-and-mars |archive-date=May 21, 2022 |access-date=March 10, 2022 |magazine=Vanity Fair}}</ref> Despite the pregnancy, Musk confirmed reports that the couple were "semi-separated" in September 2021; in an interview with [[Time (magazine)|''Time'']] in December 2021, he said he was single.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Ivie |first=Devon |date=September 24, 2021 |title=Elon Musk and Grimes Took the Red Pill and Broke Up |url=https://www.vulture.com/2021/09/elon-musk-and-grimes-break-up-after-3-years-together.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210924171854/https://www.vulture.com/2021/09/elon-musk-and-grimes-break-up-after-3-years-together.html |archive-date=September 24, 2021 |access-date=September 28, 2021 |work=Vulture}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=September 24, 2021 |title=Elon Musk says he and partner Grimes are semi-separated |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-58684724 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210928064543/https://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-58684724 |archive-date=September 28, 2021 |access-date=September 28, 2021 |publisher=[[BBC News]] }}</ref> In October 2023, Grimes sued Musk over parental rights and custody of X Æ A-Xii.<ref>{{cite news |date=November 11, 2023 |title=Grimes Says Elon Musk Evaded Being Served With Child Custody Papers At Least 12 Times |url=https://www.huffpost.com/entry/grimes-says-elon-musk-evaded-being-served-with-child-custody-papers-at-least-12-times_n_654f920ce4b0c9f24660475c |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240217191409/https://www.huffpost.com/entry/grimes-says-elon-musk-evaded-being-served-with-child-custody-papers-at-least-12-times_n_654f920ce4b0c9f24660475c |archive-date=February 17, 2024 |access-date=April 21, 2024 |website=HuffPost}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=December 7, 2023 |title=Elon Musk Drags Grimes' Tweets Into Increasingly Nasty Custody Battle |url=https://futurism.com/the-byte/elon-musk-grimes-tweets-custody |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231216111458/https://futurism.com/the-byte/elon-musk-grimes-tweets-custody |archive-date=December 16, 2023 |access-date=April 21, 2024 |publisher=Futurism}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=Musk Sued By Ex-Girlfriend Grimes Over Parental Rights: Report |url=https://www.ndtv.com/feature/elon-musk-sued-by-ex-girlfriend-grimes-over-parental-rights-report-4447991 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240311001659/https://www.ndtv.com/feature/elon-musk-sued-by-ex-girlfriend-grimes-over-parental-rights-report-4447991 |archive-date=March 11, 2024 |access-date=April 21, 2024 |publisher=NDTV}}</ref> Elon Musk has taken X Æ A-Xii to multiple official events in Washington, D.C. during [[Second presidency of Donald Trump|Trump's second term in office]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chang |first=Emily |date=February 12, 2025 |title=Musk's son 'Lil X' steals spotlight in the Oval Office |url=https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/musks-son-lil-steals-spotlight-oval-office/story?id=118713138 |access-date=February 15, 2025 |website=ABC News}}</ref>

Also in July 2022, ''The Wall Street Journal'' reported that Musk allegedly had an affair with [[Nicole Shanahan]], the wife of Google co-founder [[Sergey Brin]], in 2021, leading to their divorce the following year.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Grind |first1=Kirtsen |last2=Glazer |first2=Emily |date=July 24, 2022 |title=Elon Musk's Friendship With Sergey Brin Ruptured by Alleged Affair |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/elon-musk-affair-sergey-brin-wife-divorce-11658674840?siteid=yhoof2 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220724180459/https://www.wsj.com/articles/elon-musk-affair-sergey-brin-wife-divorce-11658674840?siteid=yhoof2 |archive-date=July 24, 2022 |access-date=July 24, 2022 |work=The Wall Street Journal}}</ref> Musk denied the report.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Musil |first1=Steven |last2=Van Boom |first2=Daniel |date=July 24, 2022 |title=Elon Musk Reportedly Had Affair With Google Co-Founder's Wife |url=https://www.cnet.com/tech/elon-musk-reportedly-had-affair-with-google-co-founders-wife/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221007134334/https://www.cnet.com/tech/elon-musk-rejects-allegations-of-affair-with-sergey-brins-wife/ |archive-date=October 7, 2022 |access-date=July 25, 2022 |publisher=CNET}}</ref> Musk also had a relationship with Australian actress [[Natasha Bassett]], who has been described as "an occasional girlfriend".{{sfn|Isaacson|2023|pp=7, 265}} In October 2024, ''The New York Times'' reported Musk bought a Texas compound for his children and their mothers,<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 29, 2024 |title=Elon Musk Wants Big Families. He Bought a Secret Compound for His. |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/29/business/elon-musk-children-compound.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241117093236/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/29/business/elon-musk-children-compound.html |archive-date=November 17, 2024 |access-date=November 19, 2024 |website=The New York Times}}</ref> though Musk denied having done so.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Siegler |first=Mara |date=October 30, 2024 |title=Exclusive {{!}} Elon Musk denies NY Times' claim of secretive family estate |url=https://pagesix.com/2024/10/30/lifestyle/elon-musk-denies-ny-times-claim-of-secretive-family-estate/ |access-date=January 21, 2025 |language=en-US}}</ref>

Musk also has four children with [[Shivon Zilis]], director of operations and special projects at [[Neuralink]]: twins born via [[In vitro fertilisation|IVF]] in 2021, a child born in 2024 via surrogacy and a child born in 2025.<ref name="Zilis">{{cite web|url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/who-is-shivon-zilis-elon-musks-partner-who-announced-birth-of-their-4th-child-101740841989650.html|title=Who is Shivon Zilis, Elon Musk's partner who announced birth of their 4th child?|work=Hindustan Times|via=HT News Desk|date=March 1, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Ankel |first=Sophia |date=August 27, 2022 |title=Elon Musk and Neuralink exec had twins via IVF, no romance: report |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-neuralink-exec-twins-via-ivf-no-romance-report-2022-8 |access-date=July 9, 2024 |website=Business Insider |language=en-US |archive-date=July 9, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240709140834/https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-neuralink-exec-twins-via-ivf-no-romance-report-2022-8 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="NYTTAU">{{cite news |last1=Szalai |first1=Jennifer |date=September 9, 2023 |title=Elon Musk Wants to Save Humanity. The Only Problem: People. |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/09/books/review/elon-musk-walter-isaacson.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20230909163003/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/09/books/review/elon-musk-walter-isaacson.html |archive-date=September 9, 2023 |access-date=September 19, 2023 |work=The New York Times}}</ref><ref name="WhoIs">{{Cite web |date=June 24, 2024 |title=Who Is Shivon Zilis? Meet the Mother of 3 of Elon Musk's 12 Children |url=https://www.eonline.com/news/1404242/who-is-shivon-zilis-meet-the-mother-of-3-of-elon-musks-12-children |access-date=July 9, 2024 |website=E! Online |archive-date=July 9, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240709140834/https://www.eonline.com/news/1404242/who-is-shivon-zilis-meet-the-mother-of-3-of-elon-musks-12-children |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Alexander |first1=Sophie |last2=Hull |first2=Dana |date=June 21, 2024 |title=Elon Wants YOU to Have More Babies |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/features/2024-elon-musk-population-collapse-baby-push/ |access-date=June 21, 2024 |publisher=[[Bloomberg News]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Elon Musk Welcomes 14th Child, His Fourth Baby with Shivon Zilis |url=https://people.com/elon-musk-welcomes-14th-child-with-shivon-zilis-11688958 |access-date=March 1, 2025 |website=People.com |language=en}}</ref> Musk allegedly had a child with author Ashley St. Clair in 2024.<ref name="Mattioli 16APR2025"/><ref>{{Cite web |title=Author Ashley St. Clair Says She Gave Birth to Elon Musk's 13th Child 5 Months Ago |url=https://people.com/elon-musk-welcomed-13th-child-5-months-ago-with-ashley-st-clair-11680525 |access-date=March 28, 2025 |website=People.com |language=en}}</ref>

On February 14, 2025, Ashley St. Clair, an influencer and author, posted on X claiming to have given birth to Musk's son Romulus five months earlier, which media outlets reported as Musk's supposed thirteenth child.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Snider |first=Mike |title=Ashley St. Clair says Elon Musk is the father of baby she had in 2024 |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/news/2025/02/17/elon-musk-ashley-st-clair-children-kids/78744733007/ |access-date=February 19, 2025 |website=USA TODAY |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=February 18, 2025 |title=Elon Musk breaks silence after MAGA influencer claims he's fathered 13th child |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/elon-musk-response-ashley-st-clair-baby-b2699865.html |access-date=February 19, 2025 |website=The Independent |language=en}}</ref> On February 22, 2025, it was reported that St Clair had filed for sole custody of her five-month-old son and for Musk to be recognised as the child's father.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Rosner |first1=Lawrence |last2=Yee |first2=Elizabeth |title=Ashley St. Clair Sues Elon Musk for Sole Legal Custody of Their Son (Exclusive) |url=https://people.com/ashley-st-clair-sues-elon-musk-for-sole-legal-custody-of-their-son-rsc-11684615 |website=People.com |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=February 23, 2025 |title=MAGA Baby Mama Says Musk Admitted Paternity in Steamy Texts |url=https://www.thedailybeast.com/maga-baby-mama-ashley-st-clair-says-elon-musk-admitted-paternity-in-steamy-text-messages/ |website=The Daily Beast |language=en}}</ref> On March 31, 2025, Musk wrote that, while he was unsure if he was the father of St. Clair's child, he had paid St. Clair $2.5 million and would continue paying her $500,000 per year.<ref>{{cite web |last=Fortinsky |first=Sarah |title=Elon Musk says he sent MAGA influencer Ashley St. Clair $2.5 million, open to paternity test |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/5224631-elon-musk-ashley-st-clair-paternity-test/ |work=The Hill |date=March 31, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Mattioli |first1=Dana |title=The Tactics Elon Musk Uses to Manage His 'Legion' of Babies—and Their Mothers |url=https://www.wsj.com/politics/elon-musk-children-mothers-ashley-st-clair-grimes-dc7ba05c |website=WSJ |date=April 16, 2025 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |author1=Mike Bedigan |title=Sources close to Elon Musk believe number of kids is much higher than publicly known |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/elon-musk-how-many-kids-b2734487.html |website=The Independent |access-date=April 16, 2025 |language=en-gb |date=April 16, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |author1=Josie Ensor |title=Elon Musk wants a 'legion' of children for apocalypse, says Ashley St Clair |url=https://www.thetimes.com/us/news-today/article/elon-musk-ashley-st-clair-children-payments-r9fgztfkz |website=www.thetimes.com |access-date=April 16, 2025 |language=en-gb |date=April 16, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Musk Only Grants 'Special Status' to One of His Many Baby Mamas |url=https://www.thedailybeast.com/elon-musk-only-grants-special-status-to-one-of-his-many-baby-mamas/ |website=The Daily Beast |language=en |date=April 16, 2025}}</ref> Later reporting from the ''Wall Street Journal'' indicated that $1 million of these payments to St. Clair was structured as a loan.<ref name="Mattioli 16APR2025" />

